{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff","id":350125,"title":"Fan-made splat display: show us your stuff!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-25T16:26:11-08:00","id":350125,"title":"Fan-made splat display: show us your stuff!","content":"So, I had some ideas for Homebrewed supernaturals, and I figured I might as well set up a thread, not just to show my ideas, but to allow everyone to share. So critique the ideas bellow or share your own!<br /> <br /> [Blank] THE INFECTED<br /> Those of this group of Supernaturals have been changed by the Disease, a strange, unnatural viral infection that causes those Infected to die or gain strange, protean supernatural powers. Inspired by Pathogen: The Infected and EmoGoth1337's Virus on RPG.net.<br /> Mood: Uncertainty-The Disease is a dangerous thing, one which can change a person into a horrendous monster, but despite the clinical terms the infected use to describe the Disease, it can grant them power unseen outside mankind's wildest imagination. Weather It is Boon or Bane can change from person to person or even day to day.<br /> <br /> Theme: Holding it together- It can be so easy to break, to fail to maintain one's Coherency and become some Thing. The Infected have to be careful and focus, because those who aren't lose their humanity very quickly. <br /> <br /> INHERENT AXIS:Vector- This is how the Infected are infected, and what subtly different incarnation of the Disease they manifest. <br /> ~VECTORS <br /> \u2022Airborne: Those infected through the air. Tend to be subtle.<br /> \u2022Savaged: Those infected through nature. Tend to be aggressive.<br /> \u2022Bloodied: Infected through humans. Tend to be social.<br /> \u2022Contaminated: Infected through objects, food, or drink. Tend to be paranoid. <br /> \u2022Tainted: Infected through inheritance. Tend to be focused.<br /> <br /> OUTSIDE AXIS: Stratagem- The survival strategy the Infected uses, focused on how they understand the Disease. More like Archetypes or Refinements than Covenants.<br /> ~STRATAGEMS<br /> \u2022 Prognosticators: AKA Docs, Medics,Quacks. Disease as mystery, seek to understand the Disease and themselves.<br /> \u2022Sentinels: AKA Heroes, Martyrs, Busybodies. Disease as Blessing, focus on using the Disease to help others.<br /> \u2022Opportunists: AKA Execs, Climbers, Piggies. Disease as Opportunity, focus on using Disease to further one's own goals.<br /> \u2022Evolutionists: AKA Bosses, Unifiers, Tyrants. Disease as Ascension, believe Disease is next step for humanity, seek to unite the Infected.<br /> \u2022Normalists: AKA Joes/Janes, Facades,Stepfords. Disease as Obstacle, seeks to maintain normalcy, see Winter Court. <br /> <br /> SUPERNATURAL ADVANTAGE: Morphism- How mutable their form is, how easy it is to activate Symptoms.<br /> <br /> INTEGRITY STAT: Coherency- How much the Infected controls their form, how easy it is to appear human, weakened by forsaking humanity or using powers too often. <br /> <br /> POWERS: Symptoms- Mutations that can be manifested, weak ones subtle, strong ones blatant, lower Coherency makes even subtle ones more obvious, high Morphism and Low Coherency makes it harder to stick to human appearance.<br /> <br /> AVATAR: THE ELDRITCH<br /> Those of this group of Supernaturals were once normal people... Until they realized they weren't real. They were instead Avatars, extruded bits of pseudo-selves created by inscrutable, unknown entities from outside our world.<br /> <br /> MOOD: Desperate Hunger- The Eldritch are born empty and hollow, lacking the selfhood others take for granted. Their entire existence is built around this hunger, the fear that they are not &quot;real&quot; enough, and that they will fade away into the nothing they were formed from. <br /> <br /> THEME: Search for Identity- The Avatars are born empty. They were created as hollow masks, and their very existence is based around making themselves someone who truly exists. Their whole &quot;culture&quot; ,such as it is, is dedicated to this pursuit. <br /> <br /> INHERENT AXIS: Origin-Maybe there are only a few of these Entities, or maybe there are simply a few categories, but the Eldritch notice a few similarities in their natures, which manifest at their worst the less Selfhood they have. I'm unsure what they should be. On one hand, the Origins could be twisted, Lovecraftian twists on traditional roles in mythologic pantheons(for example, a fertility/love god(ess) who represent poisoned , self-destructive emotion and fertility without sanity or limits. Also, maybe a Patriarch figure filtered through the Daemon Sultan, or a Messenger/Trickster figure filtered through the Crawling Chaos. Alternatively, they could be based on the three attribute categories: The Potent(Power), The Twisting(Finesse) and the Undying(Resistance). <br /> <br /> OUTSIDE AXIS: Actualization- Again, a more philosophy based Axis, this is what the Avatar uses as the backbone of their new Identity. Currently I have:<br /> \u2022The Unchallenged:&quot;I am defined by my ability to effect others&quot;, the Pillar of Power<br /> \u2022The Passionate: &quot;I am defined by what I believe&quot;, the Pillar of Dogma<br /> \u2022The Extrophile: &quot;I am defined by those around me&quot;, the Pillar of Others<br /> \u2022The Bound: &quot;I am defined by what I am not&quot;, the Pillar of Fetters<br /> <br /> SUPERNATURAL ADVANTAGE: Distance- The Potency of the Eldritch is defined by Distance; both how far from their &quot;fellow&quot; humans as well as from the strange beings which gave them life.<br /> <br /> INTEGRITY STAT: Selfhood- While the Arisen focus on their Memory and Prometheans seek to forge their Humanity, the Avatars must focus on the creation of a true self, apart from what they were created by and the mad urges that spawned them. <br /> <br /> POWERS: Inheritance- Though they are at least separate enough from their creators to develop their own identities, they still possess a number of strange sorceries and alien powers they euphemistically call Inheritances. These powers can be made stronger through ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T20:54:34-08:00","id":350357,"title":"","content":"Ha, I started Pathogen. I am always happy that someone is doing something with the material. Last night I spent a long time thinking about a powers system where one &quot;generalized&quot; power can then be &quot;evolved&quot; into something more specific and powerful - like demon's Gadgets + Interlocks, except getting stronger and more specific with each iteration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T08:01:47-08:00","id":350657,"title":"","content":"well, I am working on a fan splat called <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/266404-conjurer-basic-level-fan-splat\">Conjurer</a>, which is a mix between time travelers, abyssal summonings and a lot of Alice in Wonderland imageries just for fun. I have invested a lot of effort into it, and I'm still not even half way to finish it :P<br /> <br /> I'm also tinkered about a revision of the Changing Breeds, which could be found in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33067-ancients-awaken-the-old-ones-chronicles-changing-breeds-discussion-brainstorming\">here</a>, and more especially a kinda antagonistic breed of atavistic shifters based around the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/326192-setting-material-the-old-ones\">Old Ones</a> (not Lovecraft's). Some other things I would like to finally write down are a template for &quot;evolved Hosts&quot; (which would be likely be based around the Shapeshifter template from WAtP), the Spirit Devourers (which are what happens when a spirit tries to claim something bigger then it can chew, would be based around the siten uzu like claimed), Fetches (as,working without a changeling counterpart), and the Second Children from the Pain Prophet's testament (which would be something like cryptids on steroids with some demonic and angelic qualities). Plus, a setting hack to play aliens which is based around what we got from Mirrors, Demon and Changeling, and converting the demons from Monte Cook's WoD under the name of Intruders.<br /> <br /> Finally, there are few ideas left on the concept level or finishing works other people did that I liked- making the demons from <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20120831032811/http://wiki.white-wolf.com/worldofdarkness/index.php?title=Demon:_The_Promised\" target=\"_blank\">Demon the Promised</a> into something playable, making a playable Sublimati, expanded abmortals, kereboi sin eaters, creating an &quot;Eternal Ice&quot; counterparts to Promethean, expanding some ideas for fan games I ran to in the internet (sorcerer, daemon and warlock) and adding Tulpas, Ophidians, Black Dogs, Exorcists and Lidrecs.<br /> <br /> Yeah, no way in hell I'm gonna finish them all :P<br /> <br /> EDIT: also, something like magi's Djinn. still thinking how it could be adapted into horror :P<br /> Also- Gargoyles and Revenants","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 12-26-2014, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T01:06:56-08:00","id":354549,"title":"","content":"Well, I've been batting around a few ideas, but I really don't know which one would be most appealing to players, or which I should probably focus on developing, or even if they're worth developing...<br /> <br /> <u><b>Celestial: The Reclamation</b></u><br /> You were a god once--a Celestial. You were an Olympian sitting on your golden throne high atop your mountain, maintaining order in the world. You were a Deva sitting in your shining palace in the Heavens, passing judgement and brining balance to the cycle of life. You were a Grigori flying high in the skies, teaching and guiding humanity towards a brighter future on behalf of Heaven. The world was once bright and full of possibilities--and then you fucked it all up.<br /> <br /> Your selfish and petty actions led to the creation of a child which overthrew the gods from their mountain; you're wasteful and negligent focus caused you to burn through your merit and you fell from your shining palaces in the heavens; you became distracted, eventually shirking your duties and bringing forth the great flood which nearly destroyed the world and forever banned you from your place in Heaven. You were a god once--immortal, all-powerful, and all but invincible\u2026but now you walk in the modern nights a mere shadow of your former self. This is a World of Darkness, and it's YOUR FAULT. You move across the planet now, hunted by creatures that once feared and worshipped you, trying desperately to pick up the pieces of your former glory all in the quest of that one seemingly impossible goal\u2026redemption.<br /> <br /> <u>Celestial</u>, a game of sorrow and lost majesty, where fallen gods seek reclamation: a way to right their wrongs and put the world the way it once was.<br /> <br /> [Side Note: No Celestials aren't quite the gods of myth, but rather they're the beings which inspired those stories, along with their prophecies of doom and despair--all stories which relate to how the WoD became the WoD]<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Keres: The Consummation</u></b><br /> It all began with the choice. It might've been in a dark alley on your way home, or perhaps it was in but a dream on an otherwise unremarkable day, or perhaps you saw him in the darkness of death after you were murdered\u2026But it all ended the same. HE came. The man whose face and voice you can't remember, dressed in a black dress suit. He said his name was Moira, he said he had an offer for you. You would serve as an agent of Fate. You would serve for a set period of time, do as you were commanded, kill as ordered, destroy as directed.<br /> <br /> If you followed your orders, if you survived to the end, you would be granted the Prize. The Prize was different for each person--perhaps they wanted revenge on the person who ruined their family's good name, perhaps they wanted a happy life with their soul mate, perhaps they wanted to see their murdered daughter alive and well again--but what it all boiled down to was what was most precious to you. The Prize was your heart's desire. No tricks, no traps, no twist endings\u2026whatever you truly wanted, delivered.<br /> <br /> Now you're one of the Keres, an agent of Fate. By day you try to maintain a semi-normal life as a mundane human being. But by night you transform into a terrifying weapon of kismet, bringing death and destruction whenever it is commanded of you. And you must obey the orders that ring in your head, you must obey them as close to the letter as possible, if you want your Prize. Furthermore, if you fail to regularly follow through with what is commanded of you, or you are slain in your duties, something worse than death awaits you.<br /> <br /> Yet, you struggle...<br /> <br /> Sure you slay monsters and other corrupt influences in the world, but what of the seemingly innocent lives you are asked to reap? What of the apparently good organizations and people you are asked to eradicate from existence? Is that worth it?<br /> <br /> <u>Keres</u>, a game of choices and uncertainty, where souls seek the consummation towards their ultimate desire, or control over their Fate.<br /> <br /> [Side Note: Draws inspirations from things like MARVEL's <i>Ghost Rider</i>, Image Comics <i>The Crow</i>, and a little bit of the video game <i>Twisted Metal</i>, among other things]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","user":"hellovg","date":". 08-06-2015, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T05:41:27-08:00","id":354686,"title":"","content":"@hellovg:Both of those are pretty awesome! I especially like how Celestial seems like it would focus on more &quot;titanic&quot; heroes, more Kronus than Zeus. Any ideas for the Internal or External Axises(or Splats, as others call them) for that or Keres?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T20:05:24-08:00","id":355357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=354686#post354686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any ideas for the Internal or External Axises(or Splats, as others call them) for that or Keres?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, nothing official yet. For <u>Celestial</u> the Inherent axis revolves around what their former domain was in times past--The first group ruled in the heavens, and hold an affinity for powers dealing with energy and physics, as well as such concepts such as honor and justice. The second group ruled in the elements (ocean and mountain gods and such) and hold an affinity for the elements as well as for spirits and numina. The third group ruled amongst mortals and animals (trickster and hearth gods and such) and hold an affinity for luck, illusions, and emotions and such. The final group ruled in the realms of the dead, and hold affinity to dark and occult forces as well as spirits of the departed. <br /> <br /> For <u>Keres</u>, I've had the darndest time deciding their inherent axis and how they should be divided up. <br /> <br /> I haven't formulated outside axis for either group, nor have I any idea how their power would work, or what their powers would be called.<br /> <br /> Comments?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T04:34:54-08:00","id":355632,"title":"","content":"I do have a concept for a Psychic game themed around the conflict between individuality and the needs of society and web culture. However I haven't even started working on it beyond writing the outline. I know how much investment writing a fanline takes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T11:59:33-08:00","id":355930,"title":"","content":"One thing I've been working on for a while is a sci-fi inspired rule set, with templates for full body cyborgs, more genetically themed transhumans, uploaded minds, and just plain ol people making the most out of a cyberbrain or something. I don't have much in the way of solid mechanics just yet, only the general idea that I want to differentiate it from Bleeding Edge's Plugins by having a more &quot;iPhone&quot;ish approach, with an emphases on making the most out of a few major implants or technologies and improving their capabilities with experienced usage and some tinkering/programing, along with some kind of superhuman merit system to reflect those who've practiced using their transhuman attributes. <br /> <br /> But wait, there's more! I've also been poking at a system for playing starships and mechs. The Mechs would probably be a simple attribute-replacement, with the pilot providing the skills and some additional things. The ships though are a bit more complex as I'm trying to cobble together some kind of ramshackle tabletop EvE online (which I think was once stated to be a thing but now isn't). While it's kind of inspired by Infinite Macabre's ship rules, I'd like to try to make something that's more complex and robust for the more space-based stories, and because I think I like trying to make splats. <br /> <br /> So far, this is a bit more worked out, and I'm just going to go ahead and <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NYRSksKx33_zQd-JW5ahn0gaBb814viTvnJqFa4Q2jI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">post what I have so far</a> for possible commentary. <br /> <br /> Obviously this is all still a long way from even being remotely playable, and to be honest, I doubt I'll poke at the mechanics more until I figure out the thematic side of my take on sci-fi cyberpunk and space opera. I should note that I'm thinking of all this independently of the World of Darkness. For now, I'm working on this as if are no things like vampires and mages and such in the mix, no God-Machines except for the ones built by hyperintelegent madmen that are probably faulty and brilliantly idiotic, which IMO would make them more terrifying.<br /> <br /> Instead, I'm more interested in the idea of Intelligence Amplification, exploring the implications of people augmenting their minds and bodies in the context of all the conflicting cultures subcultures and attitudes that we see today. Most people will want to just be their own thing and not harm anyone else, just a plain ol person with their own quirks. Others will probably be monsters. Some will be both. While there are horrible aliens out there, I like the idea of most of the monsters having human origins that driven more by lofty goals and plain ol hate, though I also want to at least try to rethink that tired and frankly dumb trope of &quot;cybernetics eat your humanity.&quot; <br /> <br /> To use an Eclipse Phase comparison (because I know someone will): less focus on the Exsurgent ETI and TITAN scale AIs, more focus on Exhumans and Factors. Technically I could do all this in EP, but to be honest I like the Storytelling system better.<br /> <br /> Admitdly I could do all this on Future!Earth, but I loved Star Trek as a kid and it's my damn setting, so fuck it. Besides, I like the idea of a setting that's &quot;Star Trek + Elysium&quot;, not to mention it could provide for some cool ideas if/when I put the World of Darkness back in. Vampire ships? Space battles with a supernal angel? A ship crewed by a single hive-souled? A cyborg building his own golden road? I think it could be cool. <br /> <br /> In short, there's lots of ambitious ideas but I'm still trying to give the whole thing it's own spin, as I still feel like it's very much &quot;this thing from another franchise, BUT WITH THIS!&quot; I also feel like this post will be the odd one out in this thread considering the lack of supernatural anything going on, but I still feel like it has a horror inspiration that's fitting with the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/671-the-lone-gunman","name":"The Lone Gunman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T13:03:00-08:00","id":358539,"title":"","content":"Had an idea a bit before Demon the Descent was Released.<br /> <br /> &quot;Angel: The Ethereal&quot;<br /> <br /> Your a Angel serving on Earth trying to balance your duties to God based on the &quot;Kommandments&quot;<br /> <br /> with your human like emotions.<br /> <br /> God Freuently commands Unpleasant or even reprehensible actions, so long as the <i>net effect</i>, will be positive.<br /> <br /> For the morality trait I did decide this much that at 10 Your actualy a borderline Sociopath, albeit one without greed or malice.<br /> <br /> at lower scores, for good or ill, your driven more by human emotions, rather then Divine purpose.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T08:16:48-08:00","id":364418,"title":"","content":"WAY back when, I wrote up my take on Parasite Eve in the nWoD, and I've updated it for second edition (still haven't finished the Third Birthday Chronicle part, mostly because the game failed to grab me. . . I may completely jettison that aspect and go on the seeds I already wrote that are more interesting to me.)<br /> <br /> For those who are unaware, Parasite Eve and Parasite Eve II were games for the Playstation. The basic story was that mitochondria, symbiotic organisms that provide the energy our cells need to function, mutated and evolved into something else, called Neo-Mitochondria. They caused horrific transformations in their hosts, resulting in dangerous monsters called Neo-Mitochondrial Creatures (or NMCs.) The NMCs were led by Eve. Formerly a singer named Melissa Pearce, Eve was the result of Neo-Mitochondria transforming a human host. Eve claimed to be a sapient being older than humanity, who had been guiding evolution for thousands of years to bring about her rise and the end of &quot;nucleic domination.&quot; Whether this was true, or simply a delusion of Eve's warped mind, no one can say.<br /> <br /> There was one other human infected with Neo-Mitochondria. Police Detective Aya Brea. But unlike Melissa Pearce, her Neo-Mitochondria did not warp her body and destroy her mind. Aya was able to channel her Neo-Mitochondrial energy in any number of ways, and was instrumental in stopping Eve. She continues to hunt NMCs with an offshoot of the FBI, the Mitochondria Investigation and Suppression Team, MIST.<br /> <br /> There aren't X or Y Axis in my PE book. Characters can be normal humans, or NMHs (Neo-Mitochondrial Humans.) There are two kinds of NMHs, Infected and Activated. Neo-Mitochondria is the result of mad science tampering with already-evolving mitochondria, and some humans have mitochondria in their bodies on similar evolutionary tracks. They can be awakened into full NMHs by close proximity to concentrations of Neo-Mitochondrial energy. Infected NMHs were attacked by ANMCs (Artifical Neo-Mitochondrial Creatures), and the parasites infected them to turn them into ANMCs as well. A stabilizing vaccine, developed from the mitochondria of activated NMHs, allows them to (mostly) retain control of their human forms.<br /> <br /> <b>Theme:</b> Distrust, Secrecy, and the Monsters Within. NMHs look just like everyone else. . until they immolate dozens of monsters with a wave of their hand, or transform into a monster themselves. Eve was just an ordinary, if slightly sickly, young woman before she became the omnicidal maniac Eve. If Eve was the ancient consciousness she claims to be, can anyone be certain the NMHs have slipped her control, or are they puppets dancing on invisible strings? If Eve was just a delusion of a Neo-Mitochondrial fractured mind, then who's to say no other NMH won't suffer the same psychosis? To avoid public panic, the existence of Neo-Mitochondria and NMCs is kept tightly controlled. But when scorpions the size of go-karts start attacking people in broad daylight, secrecy becomes a difficult thing.<br /> <br /> <b>Power Stat:</b> Parasite Energy. As Parasite Energy increases, NMHs become more powerful, able to perform greater feats with their Neo-Mitochondrial Energy, but the more other people begin to fear their power, and the farther from humanity they set themselves apart.<br /> <br /> <b>Power Pool:</b> Mitochondria Points. Term taken straight from the video game because I couldn't think of anything better, explained in-universe as what NMH's refer to the energy generated by their Neo-Mitochondria because any other term to describe it requires at least two doctorates to pronounce.<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity Stat:</b> Integrity. NMH's are still human. . . probably.<br /> <br /> <b>Powers:</b> Parasite Powers. Broken into five categories, Air, Earth, Fire, Water, and Transformation. Transformation powers are only attainable by infected NMHs, and are crucial to controlling their ANMC forms and harnessing the vast power contained within.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T14:28:26-08:00","id":364784,"title":"","content":"I worked on the beautiful trainwreck that was Outsider: the Calling, an nWoD game about normal people touched by the Cthulhu Mythos. <br /> <br /> There were five different origins (Cthulhu, Yog-Sothoth, Shub-Nighurath, Nyarlathotep, and Hastur) that had great fluff, with the other axis being your response to the transformation (eager for revenge, trying to become normal again, faithful servitude, etc). Powers were called Rejections and were super neat in that they operated on the inverse of Mage's paradox; everything they did had to be blatantly impossible. There was talk of including the Dreamlands, there was discussion of interesting settings across the globe, we wrote up specific Hunter groups, it had a Cult mechanic long before Mummy...<br /> <br /> The rules were terrible. And the project hasn't updated in three years (as you might expect from an anonymous 4chan collaboration). But the ideas were a lot of fun, and I turned a lot of that into Arkham Lost, my C:tL setting hack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T14:42:17-08:00","id":364797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=364784#post364784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I worked on the beautiful trainwreck that was Outsider: the Calling, an nWoD game about normal people touched by the Cthulhu Mythos.<br /> <br /> There were five different origins (Cthulhu, Yog-Sothoth, Shub-Nighurath, Nyarlathotep, and Hastur) that had great fluff, with the other axis being your response to the transformation (eager for revenge, trying to become normal again, faithful servitude, etc). Powers were called Rejections and were super neat in that they operated on the inverse of Mage's paradox; everything they did had to be blatantly impossible. There was talk of including the Dreamlands, there was discussion of interesting settings across the globe, we wrote up specific Hunter groups, it had a Cult mechanic long before Mummy...<br /> <br /> The rules were terrible. And the project hasn't updated in three years (as you might expect from an anonymous 4chan collaboration). But the ideas were a lot of fun, and I turned a lot of that into Arkham Lost, my C:tL setting hack.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I remember seeing some of that, there were lot of fun ideas. You should get back into it, especially now with the 2e rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T14:52:34-08:00","id":364805,"title":"","content":"@atamajakki: I remember seeing that! I thought it was a neat idea, though I'd have done something different for the External Axis, mostly because my close-minded self having trouble imagining the non-Rebels as anything other than villains(Rebels, of course, I can imagine as both heroes and villains).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T19:21:51-08:00","id":364993,"title":"","content":"I doubt there's enough functional material in O:tC (I still remember when it was <i>Alien: the Outsider</i>, oh my goodness) to justify a 2e, as there never really <i>was</i> a 1e; anything I'd be doing, I'd essentially be building the game completely fresh. I just don't have that in me.<br /> <br /> As I mentioned, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/168334-arkham-lost\">Arkham Lost</a> was my attempt to salvage <i>Outsider</i>'s best ideas; it doesn't hurt that the game already had a lot of shared thematic content with Changeling to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T21:03:16-08:00","id":369386,"title":"","content":"Well, a friend of mine and myself are working on (yet another) Dragon fanline, since we were dissatisfied with Embers. Basically, our thought was that no Dragon game could succeed at making &quot;being a dragon&quot; horrific. Like, at the end of the day, dragons eating each other's hearts for power sounds horrific, until you realize that what you've made is essentially Highlander with Dragons. That's not a horror game, that's a metal album cover. So our goal is to make a Dragon game that's a metal album cover right from the start. So, I present for your consideration:<br /> <br /> <b>Dragon: the Inheritance</b><br /> <br /> You are a dragon, and you love it. And really, what isn't there to love? You are strong, you are deadly, you can even fly unaided through the sky. The poor normal people tremble in terror at your passing, for you are the embodiment of everything that has ever preyed upon mankind, and they know it. Dragons have always been a symbol of greed and arrogance, but with all the power you hold in your claws, why shouldn't you be? Why shouldn't you rule the world?<br /> <br /> The answer is that once, you did. Or, at least, your distant ancestors did. Before the age of man, dragons were the planet's dominant species. They had their own great cities and civilization, and the humans were lowly, primitive servants. Until, that is, they rose up against their rightful rulers. Just as the dragons had once usurped another race, the Cycle of Fate turned, and humans overthrew the dragons. Because of the actions of a great sorcerer, however, the dragons were not wiped from the earth, but instead were disguised as humans and left to hide in the shadows of the world. <br /> <br /> Dragons are now thought of as myths and tall tales, populating the various legends of mankind. And those legends contain seeds of truth about their subjects. Dragons do hoard things that are precious to them, though not always in forms as recognizable as piles of gold. Dragons can, at will, change from their human disguises to their awesome true forms. And, inevitably, any story involving a dragon ends with the dragon being slain.<br /> <br /> You see, normally when a dragon reveals its true form to mortals, an effect called the Enkindling occurs which causes those mortals to react with fear and awe. But sometimes, the Enkindling produces the opposite effect, creating a mortal who will try, at any costs, to kill the dragon. These mortals are called Slayers, and they are the bane of a dragon's existence. Fate works on the Slayer's side, aiding their strikes and protecting them from harm. They are not unstoppable - a dragon might kill a single Slayer, or even dozens over her lifetime, but one will get to her eventually. A dragon's life is ultimately about learning to survive as long as possible, without giving up what makes them who they are.<br /> <br /> <b>Inherent Axis: Heritage</b><br /> A dragon's Heritage defines what manner of mythical dragon they are most similar to, and what they <span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">hoard.</span></span> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Amphiteres: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Divine dragons who hoard prestige.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Drakes: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Poisonous dragons who hoard aesthetic.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Hydras: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Nigh-immortal dragons who hoard experiences.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Wyverns: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Hungry, destructive dragons who hoard reputation.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Wyrms: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mystical dragons who hoard power.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Outside Axis: Dynasty</b><br /> A dragon's Dynasty is the dragon's political faction, which informs their strategy for surviving slayers. Dragons usually join the dynasty of the dragon they received their Inheritance from. <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Nagaraja: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spies and activists with command of snakes. Survival through knowledge. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Xiuhcoatl: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fire-and-brimstone dragon fight club. Survival through strength.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Yinglong: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Weather-controlling dragon mafia. Survival through resources.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Zalciai: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Luck-blessed matriarchal puppet masters. Survival through community.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Zmaj: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Sorcerous assassins with a collective messiah complex. Survival through control.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Supernatural Advantage: Kauchaomai </b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">(Ancient Greek, lit. &quot;I boast&quot;)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A dragon doesn't draw their power from any external source, but rather their own supernaturally enhanced sense of self-worth. A dragon, an Heir, is Willpower personified. They declare that they are a mighty being of scales, wings, and claws, and the universe has no choice but to comply. As such, the size and power of a dragon's true form is dependent on the strength of that dragon's conviction.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">There is no &quot;juice stat&quot; associated with Kauchaomai. Instead, it grants an extra Willpower pool to the dragon, and a dragon's activated powers cost WP points. Dragons also have an extra way to regain WP, by spending time with their hoard. The bigger the hoard, the more WP the dragon can gain.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Modified Integrity Stat: Serenity</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If a dragon's self-worth is the fuel for their power, then their self-image is the focus for that power. In order to leverage their power effectively, a dragon needs to know who they are, as a person. Even more importantly, they need to try their hardest to live up to that idealized image of themselves. Because when a dragon's actions diverge too greatly from what they feel they should be, they can lose control over their own power. Serenity measures how well a dragon knows who they should be and how well they measure up to that image, and directly effects how often they Enkindle Slayers.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Powers: Legacies</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Legacies are modifications to a dragon's true form, enhancing their natural abilities and granting them new ones. Deadly claws, armored hide, fire breath, wings, silvered tongue, poison, etc. Legacies consist of two parts: Core and Auxiliary benefits. Core benefits are simple, giving straightforward abilities on a 1-5 dot scale. Auxiliary benefits are optional add-on powers that give more specific enhancements to the core power, or provide other related benefits. (for example, immunity to fire and heat as an auxiliary to fire breath)<br /> [Essentially, a dragon's magic powers are &quot;being a motherfucking dragon.&quot;]<br /> Dragons also have access to draconic sorcery, following the example of the legendary dragon sorcerer Zirnitra.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> (Incidentally, yes, we are aware of how similar Slayers are to Beast: the Primordial's Heroes. I swear we had the idea before they even announced that they were working on a new game.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T21:59:22-08:00","id":369440,"title":"","content":"You know, there's probably more horror in &quot;no matter what I do, I will end up murdered&quot; than &quot;Highlander with Dragons&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T22:35:00-08:00","id":369461,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;Well, children, gather around and allow me to tell you a little story...&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Once upon a time, a younger, more precocious (AKA a year younger) Reaper Verse set off to start a fan splat known as <b><i>Shadow: The Perverse</i></b>. Given that he had written a few pages in a fit of mania and sudden inspiration, the style was overall clunky but showed promise. Unfortunately, life happened and prevented him from continuing his work in a consistent pattern, thus cursing the fan splat to the depths of his Documents folder.<br /> <br /> In all seriousness, I wanted to approach the World of Darkness splats by writing a creature that was deliberately patterned off of Eastern culture, focusing on Taoism and the idea of Yin and Yang as well as the myriad creatures and the theoretical person we as humans believe others view us as. Mainly, <i><b>Shadows</b></i> were creatures of hate and self-loathing that were spontaneously born whenever a human had a personal crisis. They were essentially a negative version of humanity that lived in a land that did not exist known as <i><b>The Labyrinth</b></i>. They had no reason to exist but did and were envious of their mortal counterparts for having some reason to live their own lives. <br /> <br /> What I did not post were my current thoughts about Shadows, mainly that, because they are creatures that should not exist, they are constantly pained by a void in their soul, seeking to fill that void by feeding on human misery. If they didn't, they would be reconsumed by the void that exists beyond the material realm and The Labyrinth.<br /> <br /> In a nutshell, <i><b>Kingdom Hearts'</b></i> Nobodies, <b><i>Silent Hill's </i></b>gallery of iconic monsters, and <b><i>Persona's</i></b> Shadows all wrapped into one neat little package. Pity that I gave up for a bit. At least now I can scavenge the cutting room floor bits and continue with some insight. :V","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T07:10:43-08:00","id":369723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=369440#post369440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, there's probably more horror in &quot;no matter what I do, I will end up murdered&quot; than &quot;Highlander with Dragons&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes. I suppose what I said was a little bit misleading. Our goal wasn't exactly to make a WoD game that wasn't a horror game, it was to make one where your life doesn't inherently suck because of what you are. External horror, not internal. Or, to put it another way, more like Demon and Mummy than Vampire and Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T08:59:18-08:00","id":369782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Tin Soldier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=369723#post369723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yes. I suppose what I said was a little bit misleading. Our goal wasn't exactly to make a WoD game that wasn't a horror game, it was to make one where your life doesn't inherently suck because of what you are. External horror, not internal. Or, to put it another way, more like Demon and Mummy than Vampire and Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>The horror is extremely internal in Mummy. Demon doesn't do it the same way, but there's still a lot of horror around the concept of being hunted all the time, not being a real person, feeling afraid that your inability to innately express your emotions marks you as a sociopath, among other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T09:33:35-08:00","id":369799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=369782#post369782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The horror is extremely internal in Mummy. Demon doesn't do it the same way, but there's still a lot of horror around the concept of being hunted all the time, not being a real person, feeling afraid that your inability to innately express your emotions marks you as a sociopath, among other things.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://gifrific.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/06/Michael-Scott-angry-stare-at-toby.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Is anyone going to comment on the splat itself, or are you just going to keep nitpicking my commentary?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2449,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","user":"One Tin Soldier","date":". 01-14-2015, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T09:49:04-08:00","id":369816,"title":"","content":"Oops, I just meant that as a compliment in the &quot;you made a game that seems like a better horror game than the other.&quot; I kinda like the Heritage and the Dynasty splits - they seem pretty interesting.<br /> <br /> I'd say that Kauchaomai should just add directly to your Willpower; maybe it should even set it to the same progression as, say, a Vampire's Vitae (so someone with Kauchaomai \u2022\u2022 would be running around with 12 Permanent Willpower). Or, heck, use that increased cap to represent how much <i>temporary Willpower</i> they can hold, and require that they ruminate on their hoard (or burn villages or whatever) to get Willpower back beyond their Permanent Willpower. Maybe let them use their Vice as well, but only if they do it while they're a FRIKKIN' DRAGON, and only if they do it <i>big</i>.<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <br /> Steve is a FRIKKIN' DRAGON with Kauchaomai \u2022, Resolve \u2022\u2022\u2022, and Composure \u2022; his Virtue is Hopeful and his Vice is Arrogant. His Willpower would be written like so: x/4(10), with x representing the amount he has right now. Let's say he's currently at one Willpower and he fulfils his Virtue; he'd fill up to four Willpower, and wouldn't get any more Willpower from fulfilling his Virtue. If he then went home and surveyed his horde, he'd recover some Willpower; if he turned into a motherfucking <i>dragon</i> and proceeded to rampage up and down the streets, commanding the pathetic mortals to <i>grovel and worship his magnificence</i>... he'd recover Willpower for his Vice.<br /> <br /> Maybe even build it from the same system as recovering Willpower from your Hoard - you get one Willpower as a base, but get back extra Willpower if the hoard (or display) is particularly large, impressive, terrifying, etcetera. You get one extra Willpower for each that applies, but can grab a Merit that increases that to two for hitting certain &quot;notes&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T11:31:17-08:00","id":369892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=369816#post369816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oops, I just meant that as a compliment in the &quot;you made a game that seems like a better horror game than the other.&quot; I kinda like the Heritage and the Dynasty splits - they seem pretty interesting.<br /> <br /> I'd say that Kauchaomai should just add directly to your Willpower; maybe it should even set it to the same progression as, say, a Vampire's Vitae (so someone with Kauchaomai \u2022\u2022 would be running around with 12 Permanent Willpower). Or, heck, use that increased cap to represent how much <i>temporary Willpower</i> they can hold, and require that they ruminate on their hoard (or burn villages or whatever) to get Willpower back beyond their Permanent Willpower. Maybe let them use their Vice as well, but only if they do it while they're a FRIKKIN' DRAGON, and only if they do it <i>big</i>.<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <br /> Steve is a FRIKKIN' DRAGON with Kauchaomai \u2022, Resolve \u2022\u2022\u2022, and Composure \u2022; his Virtue is Hopeful and his Vice is Arrogant. His Willpower would be written like so: x/4(10), with x representing the amount he has right now. Let's say he's currently at one Willpower and he fulfils his Virtue; he'd fill up to four Willpower, and wouldn't get any more Willpower from fulfilling his Virtue. If he then went home and surveyed his horde, he'd recover some Willpower; if he turned into a motherfucking <i>dragon</i> and proceeded to rampage up and down the streets, commanding the pathetic mortals to <i>grovel and worship his magnificence</i>... he'd recover Willpower for his Vice.<br /> <br /> Maybe even build it from the same system as recovering Willpower from your Hoard - you get one Willpower as a base, but get back extra Willpower if the hoard (or display) is particularly large, impressive, terrifying, etcetera. You get one extra Willpower for each that applies, but can grab a Merit that increases that to two for hitting certain &quot;notes&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, thank you! I see what you meant now.<br /> <br /> And yes, Kauchaomai does increase the amount of WP points you can spend. The only difference is that you can't spend them as willpower dots. And the progression, as we have it now, is simply 1 extra WP per dot of Kauchaomai. Adding a scaling progression would probably result in the characters having so many points that the recovery mechanics don't matter.<br /> <br /> As for Hoard, it's built as a Merit with a dot rating 1-5, and by spending a scene basking in your hoard, you regain WP points equal to the dot rating. Dot rating, of course, indicates the quality and/or size of your hoard. Virtue and Vice give you WP as per normal. (With Virtue refilling your entire pool.) <br /> <br /> While we can always tweak things, especially after we get a chance to actually playtest the game, we think that the costs are pretty solid where they are. For that matter, we have a good 45 pages of material on a google doc, I could send you a link if you're interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T11:45:53-08:00","id":369911,"title":"","content":"@Reaper Verse: Sounds like a neat idea! Any bits and pieces of ideas you could scrounge up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T11:56:18-08:00","id":369946,"title":"","content":"Ooh, send me a link! I might end up testing out the Willpower thing I suggested on my own.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I had a vague idea for a Fansplat a while back called <b>Naiad</b><b>: The &lt;Whatever&gt;</b> (never did come up with a good subtitle). You played as water spirits, and your Fuel Stat and your Integrity Equivalent were the same thing (called <b>Water</b>). So you'd have Water dots to split around effects, which might be anything from promoting growth in an area to rendering a river treacherous and &quot;hungry&quot;. More powerful powers would be a Breaking Point, since you're depleting the waters you hold inside of you; similarly, spending time in a place without water would be a Breaking Point, while being near a lake or ocean would give you a temporary boost to your Water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T12:02:15-08:00","id":369968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Tin Soldier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=369799#post369799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is anyone going to comment on the splat itself, or are you just going to keep nitpicking my commentary?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Supernatural Advantage's name is a mouthful, the fluff could use more interesting hooks and less hardlined definitions that oversimplify the condition of being something non-human within the humanist World of Darkness, and it sounds like the spoilers we've heard about Beast without the interesting hook of crossover or the versatility of the concept.<br /> <br /> One of the things that's a big part of defining the World of Darkness niche is how people react to the Condition of their circumstances. I'd daresay having every person that finds out they're not really human take it that well is sort of bizarre. How does this affect their normal relationships? What happens to a Dragon that just wants to live a human life? Is there nothing stopping them? Where's the hook?<br /> <br /> Do they start off human or do they always know they're dragons, raised by dragon families, and so on? Demon subverts the expectation of beginning human than becoming something else, but it does so in a very particular way. If your intent is to do that here, then what were they before becoming the people they are now?<br /> <br /> It sounds like you've got ideas to make a Dragon splat, but I'm not hearing what makes them compelling to play. If you can come up with some interesting hooks or ideas of how being one of these things affects you, you'll be on the right track.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T12:10:57-08:00","id":369978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=369911#post369911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Reaper Verse: Sounds like a neat idea! Any bits and pieces of ideas you could scrounge up?</div> </div> </div> </div>I still have the Word document and the original post is floating around on page 7-9. The main mechanic that the Shadows had was the ability to summon <b><i>The Fog</i></b>, a localized phenomenon that brings a section of the Labyrinth into the material world, causing physics to go all wacky and invoke strange, arbitrary rules into the world (such as preventing people from crossing passed stop signs or caution tape, opening locked doors by presenting innocuous items, and messing around with GPS and compasses), which I feel would be a selling point for the game. <br /> <br /> An idea that I'm still working through is the backstory for why the Labyrinth is, specifically the titanic lords, known as <b><i>The Guardians,</i></b> that once existed and essentially controlled the first Shadows. The main thing about them is that they are based on the <i>Ba Gua</i>, eight representations of reality, and that Shadows came to be when a Guardian known as the <b><i>Brood Mother</i></b> released them from a crevace in the land. <br /> <br /> Something that was brought up in the thread was the idea of controlling lesser Shadows, which developed into the idea of <b><i>Preta</i></b>, hungry spirits of Buddhism that suffer. I played around with this idea and came up with their counterpart, <b><i>Butterflies</i></b> that are meant to lead the Shadows in their journey to continue existing. <br /> <br /> Things that I didn't write up is their unique Splat stats. I wanted to use <b><i>Ying</i></b> and <b><i>Yang</i></b> in some manner; after reading through <i>Blood and Smoke,</i> I feel like they would work as their respective Virtue and Vice. Shadow Integrity would be something like <b><i>Existence, Identity</i></b>, or <b><i>Purpose</i></b>, meant to represent a Shadow's tie to reality; willingly abandoning things that keep them grounded to reality slowly tears at their soul until the Void consumes them, wiping them from existence.<br /> <br /> Basically, the entire idea was to play around with the idea of how the most hated aspects of individuals would behave if they were given life. Eventually, it slowly mutated into an introspective on the meaning of being &quot;real&quot; and what it means to have no actual purpose in reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T12:13:27-08:00","id":369980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Tin Soldier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=369386#post369386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, a friend of mine and myself are working on (yet another) Dragon fanline, since we were dissatisfied with Embers. Basically, our thought was that no Dragon game could succeed at making &quot;being a dragon&quot; horrific. Like, at the end of the day, dragons eating each other's hearts for power sounds horrific, until you realize that what you've made is essentially Highlander with Dragons. That's not a horror game, that's a metal album cover. So our goal is to make a Dragon game that's a metal album cover right from the start. So, I present for your consideration:</div> </div> </div> </div>Which version of dragon did you read? The first pdf, the playtest pdf, the bailout draft, the second stage pdf, the third stage half-book preview, or the thread? We've often had complaints about our setting being less than a good fit for the horror genre and we're taking measures to change that.<br /> What you are describing here is the Devourer phenomenon and it is only one component of membership in the Oroboroi. In fact, in the latest draft a dragon devouring her enemies' hearts will result in their faces clawing their way out of her body like tumors. When they surface, they're capable of speaking and they usually condemn her actions or worse tell her peers about her crimes (at which point she will be ripped to pieces if she does not escape).<br /> Also, since a human body is not meant to house a dragon's power, if an Oroboroi does not live up to the draconic ideal her heart will reject her like a bad type match and she'll turn to stone. There is that built in 'oh shit' moment when a new dragon realizes the deal that was too good to be true actually was, and her new state comes with all manner of conditions that if broken spell disaster. Finally, membership in the Oroboroi is exclusive to the point of being restrictive; the only way in is to take the credentials of another member and doing so results in their death.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I like your concept and I'd like to go through it piece by piece here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Tin Soldier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=369386#post369386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Dragon: the Inheritance</b>The answer is that once, you did. Or, at least, your distant ancestors did. Before the age of man, dragons were the planet's dominant species. They had their own great cities and civilization, and the humans were lowly, primitive servants. Until, that is, they rose up against their rightful rulers. Just as the dragons had once usurped another race, the Cycle of Fate turned, and humans overthrew the dragons. Because of the actions of a great sorcerer, however, the dragons were not wiped from the earth, but instead were disguised as humans and left to hide in the shadows of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>So your dragons are born and our dragons are made. Another member called Alastiel started a dragon project when Embers did not satisfy and strangely enough the same idea was applied: Dragons to humans instead of the other way around. So technically the two ideas are not incompatible; it would be perfectly reasonable to run a game with both Embers Oroboroi and the Inherited without resulting in a contradiction of logic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Tin Soldier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=369386#post369386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragons are now thought of as myths and tall tales, populating the various legends of mankind. And those legends contain seeds of truth about their subjects. Dragons do hoard things that are precious to them, though not always in forms as recognizable as piles of gold. Dragons can, at will, change from their human disguises to their awesome true forms. And, inevitably, any story involving a dragon ends with the dragon being slain.<br /> <br /> You see, normally when a dragon reveals its true form to mortals, an effect called the Enkindling occurs which causes those mortals to react with fear and awe. But sometimes, the Enkindling produces the opposite effect, creating a mortal who will try, at any costs, to kill the dragon. These mortals are called Slayers, and they are the bane of a dragon's existence. Fate works on the Slayer's side, aiding their strikes and protecting them from harm. They are not unstoppable - a dragon might kill a single Slayer, or even dozens over her lifetime, but one will get to her eventually. A dragon's life is ultimately about learning to survive as long as possible, without giving up what makes them who they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very interesting; it implies that whatever force displaced your dragons is still in play and actively trying to continue its work. I'm not sure fate is the best fit, but I would be interested in seeing how this plays out in your template.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Tin Soldier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=369386#post369386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Inherent Axis: Heritage</b><br /> A dragon's Heritage defines what manner of mythical dragon they are most similar to, and what they <span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">hoard.</span></span> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Amphiteres: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Divine dragons who hoard prestige.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Drakes: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Poisonous dragons who hoard aesthetic.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Hydras: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Nigh-immortal dragons who hoard experiences.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Wyverns: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Hungry, destructive dragons who hoard reputation.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Wyrms: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mystical dragons who hoard power.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I like most of this, except for the Wyrms. Don't all dragons hoard power? Perhaps you should consider reducing this axis to four options?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Tin Soldier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=369386#post369386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Outside Axis: Dynasty</b><br /> A dragon's Dynasty is the dragon's political faction, which informs their strategy for surviving slayers. Dragons usually join the dynasty of the dragon they received their Inheritance from. <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Nagaraja: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spies and activists with command of snakes. Survival through knowledge. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Xiuhcoatl: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fire-and-brimstone dragon fight club. Survival through strength.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Yinglong: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Weather-controlling dragon mafia. Survival through resources.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Zalciai: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Luck-blessed matriarchal puppet masters. Survival through community.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Zmaj: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Sorcerous assassins with a collective messiah complex. Survival through control.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>So each outside axis comes with a special power. I'm curious what Zmaj sorcery entails; it's easy to picture the others but sorcery is sort of a catch-all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Tin Soldier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=369386#post369386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Supernatural Advantage: Kauchaomai </b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">(Ancient Greek, lit. &quot;I boast&quot;)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A dragon doesn't draw their power from any external source, but rather their own supernaturally enhanced sense of self-worth. A dragon, an Heir, is Willpower personified. They declare that they are a mighty being of scales, wings, and claws, and the universe has no choice but to comply. As such, the size and power of a dragon's true form is dependent on the strength of that dragon's conviction.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">There is no &quot;juice stat&quot; associated with Kauchaomai. Instead, it grants an extra Willpower pool to the dragon, and a dragon's activated powers cost WP points. Dragons also have an extra way to regain WP, by spending time with their hoard. The bigger the hoard, the more WP the dragon can gain.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, like Conviction or Heroic Health. I like it. Have you read <b>World of Darkness Mirrors</b>? It might give you a few ideas that will help you implement this. It also might be interesting to see these dragons use more than one Willpower in a turn, perhaps abusing conventional systems (+3 to action multiple times in a turn!?!)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Tin Soldier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=369386#post369386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Powers: Legacies</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Legacies are modifications to a dragon's true form, enhancing their natural abilities and granting them new ones. Deadly claws, armored hide, fire breath, wings, silvered tongue, poison, etc. Legacies consist of two parts: Core and Auxiliary benefits. Core benefits are simple, giving straightforward abilities on a 1-5 dot scale. Auxiliary benefits are optional add-on powers that give more specific enhancements to the core power, or provide other related benefits. (for example, immunity to fire and heat as an auxiliary to fire breath)<br /> [Essentially, a dragon's magic powers are &quot;being a motherfucking dragon.&quot;]<br /> Dragons also have access to draconic sorcery, following the example of the legendary dragon sorcerer Zirnitra.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>So, sort of like the Bound in <b>Geist</b>, where the auxiliary power sources flavor the Legacy? Do you have any of these written yet? They sound interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally, I want to say that you shouldn't feel like you have to justify yourself as 'another' dragon splat. Embers hardly holds a monopoly on the concept; we are mining the myths for inspiration but dragons are an international symbol of power (both good and bad) and we don't hold claim to them simply because we started our project first. Don't let our presence inhibit you in any way and if there are systems in our game that would suit yours, go ahead and use them. That's the thing about fan projects: they're collaborative. Together we can each gain something wonderful from the other (for instance, Tempest and Embers have traded mechanics with each other and both are better because of it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T13:09:13-08:00","id":370053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Tin Soldier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=369723#post369723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yes. I suppose what I said was a little bit misleading. Our goal wasn't exactly to make a WoD game that wasn't a horror game, it was to make one where your life doesn't inherently suck because of what you are. External horror, not internal. Or, to put it another way, more like Demon and Mummy than Vampire and Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, the main horror show in Embers is highlighting the fact that the species is dying out. Going out the door. Extinct. Small embers burning against the night before they finally die out. Less highlander and more energized Wrath: The Oblivion in mood. The internal backstabbing and bickering really only serves to highlight this. &quot;congratulations, you've just eaten another dragon's heart for a small measure of power and thus driving the entire species that much closer to oblivion.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, the game is in the middle of being rewritten again and is somewhat on hiatus so hopefully we'll get the deliverance on that mood more accurately this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 01-14-2015, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T13:40:00-08:00","id":370092,"title":"","content":"@Reaper Verse: Neat! Seems like it'd be a fun idea. Not to pry, but did you have any ideas for their Internal and Social Axises?<br /> <br /> @CJC: While I can't speak for One Tin Soldier, I think from context that the Wyrms specifically hoard supernatural power: Tokens, Fetiches, spells, and whatever magic stuff dragons deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T14:19:31-08:00","id":370129,"title":"","content":"aaaargh the forum ate my original response. I'll probably write this a bit shorter than I would like to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=369980#post369980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which version of dragon did you read? The first pdf, the playtest pdf, the bailout draft, the second stage pdf, the third stage half-book preview, or the thread? We've often had complaints about our setting being less than a good fit for the horror genre and we're taking measures to change that.<br /> What you are describing here is the Devourer phenomenon and it is only one component of membership in the Oroboroi. In fact, in the latest draft a dragon devouring her enemies' hearts will result in their faces clawing their way out of her body like tumors. When they surface, they're capable of speaking and they usually condemn her actions or worse tell her peers about her crimes (at which point she will be ripped to pieces if she does not escape).<br /> Also, since a human body is not meant to house a dragon's power, if an Oroboroi does not live up to the draconic ideal her heart will reject her like a bad type match and she'll turn to stone. There is that built in 'oh shit' moment when a new dragon realizes the deal that was too good to be true actually was, and her new state comes with all manner of conditions that if broken spell disaster. Finally, membership in the Oroboroi is exclusive to the point of being restrictive; the only way in is to take the credentials of another member and doing so results in their death.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I like your concept and I'd like to go through it piece by piece here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you like it. The most recent draft of yours that we read was the one with all the art of dragons with emo hair. Which, and I mean this as helpfully as possible, you should get rid of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So your dragons are born and our dragons are made. Another member called Alastiel started a dragon project when Embers did not satisfy and strangely enough the same idea was applied: Dragons to humans instead of the other way around. So technically the two ideas are not incompatible; it would be perfectly reasonable to run a game with both Embers Oroboroi and the Inherited without resulting in a contradiction of logic. </div> </div> </div>The formal name for our Dragons is &quot;Heirs,&quot; following our theme of dragons inheriting their power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is very interesting; it implies that whatever force displaced your dragons is still in play and actively trying to continue its work. I'm not sure fate is the best fit, but I would be interested in seeing how this plays out in your template. </div> </div> </div>The Cycle of Fate is the force that ensures that ownership of the world passes from one race to the next every few millenia or so. Someone was in charge before the dragons, and someone will eventually take over after the humans. The dragons just didn't have the decency to die out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like most of this, except for the Wyrms. Don't all dragons hoard power? Perhaps you should consider reducing this axis to four options? </div> </div> </div>Wyrms, in particular, hoard power over other people. Weapon stockpiles, political clout, gang territory. Other dragons might gain these things, but none of them have the driving <i>need</i> to collect them the way Wyrms do.<br /> Wyrms also fill an important niche of being Asian Lungs or sea serpents, which is an archetype not covered by the others.<br /> For reference, Amphiteres are like Aztec couatls or the Serpent at Delphi; Drakes are the four-legged poisonous European variety; Wyverns are the two-legged devourers; and Hydras are multi-headed terrors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So each outside axis comes with a special power. I'm curious what Zmaj sorcery entails; it's easy to picture the others but sorcery is sort of a catch-all. </div> </div> </div>Zmaj-specific sorcery is control over Enkindling itself. They claim to originate from the ancient dragon sorcerer Zirnitra, who made dragons what they are today. They don't have total control, but they can shape or redirect its effects to their advantage.<br /> They also have an affinity for the Sorcery legacy, which is dragons' ritual magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmmm, like Conviction or Heroic Health. I like it. Have you read <b>World of Darkness Mirrors</b>? It might give you a few ideas that will help you implement this. It also might be interesting to see these dragons use more than one Willpower in a turn, perhaps abusing conventional systems (+3 to action multiple times in a turn!?!) </div> </div> </div>We have read Mirrors, and we are aware of how similar Kauchaomai (pronounced couch-ow-my) is to Conviction, or better yet, Arete.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, sort of like the Bound in <b>Geist</b>, where the auxiliary power sources flavor the Legacy? Do you have any of these written yet? They sound interesting. </div> </div> </div>We have all but one of the Core Legacies done, and about half of the Auxiliary Legacies. You can also PM me for the link to our doc, if you would like to look it over.<br /> <br /> In fact, same goes for anyone else in the thread. We don't want to post it publicly until we at least have a full list of powers, and when we do we'll likely make our own thread. But until then, previews are fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T15:07:04-08:00","id":370163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Tin Soldier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=370129#post370129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad you like it. The most recent draft of yours that we read was the one with all the art of dragons with emo hair. Which, and I mean this as helpfully as possible, you should get rid of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like the first PDF (That's ancient, ANCIENT news. The game has changed significantly). I scratched all of the artwork after that version and I've only just recently begun introducing images again (And admittedly the new ones need work too; they're really just there to break up walls of text). Trust me, you aren't the only person who had and has problems with the art. But I'm broke, and there's the whole matter of copyright when you go snatching images from the internet, so there aren't a whole lot of options.<br /> <br /> Thank you for clarifying the Wyrms. I'll abstain from peeking behind the curtain until you're ready to share with everybody; it's best not to poke around in the creative process until the gears are all in place, it can really muck up the works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T15:07:30-08:00","id":370164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=370092#post370092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Reaper Verse: Neat! Seems like it'd be a fun idea. Not to pry, but did you have any ideas for their Internal and Social Axises?</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries. I openly welcome prying of most to any types. <br /> <br /> The Axes did go through a bit of finagling. The main thing is that the idea of Shadow is so vague that there aren't that many archetypes that would work. Since the Shadows were meant to represent counterparts of humanity, I started with the idea of <b><i>Personae</i></b> <i>(gee, where did I get THAT word from, hint hint)</i>, archetypes that represented types of individuals such as natural leaders or walking comfort blankets and highlighting negative traits that were associated with such archetypes (leaders would be control-freaks or megalomaniacs, etc.) The naming convention was based on the Court Cards of the Tarot, going from Kings, Queens, Knights, and Pages while adding the Ace to bring the total to five (of course, I decided to flower the names up to Warlord, Consort, General, Scholar, and Herald. Why? Mainly for giggles but also to bring the idea back to an Eastern-influenced splat). Eventually, I believe I removed it because it was too...<i>obvious </i>to be used. That, and I didn't want a C&amp;D hanging over my head.<br /> <br /> The Axis that played across it was <b><i>Conceits</i></b>, the manner in which Shadows responded to their unique situation and to humanity, their existential counterpart. Because this was back in the stage in which the game was based on the Jungian concept of Shadows and Personas, the Conceits were based on the 5 (technically, I used 7) Stages of Grief. <br /> <br /> <u><i><b>SNIPPET TIME GO GO GO</b></i><br /> </u><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Conceits</b> are means in which Shadows view the world and what aspect of humanity they are to reflect. The <b>Unaware (Shock)</b> are Shadows that take on the feeling of naivety, the overall complacency to the world and the disdain to change, the inability to respond or adapt to the unknown, the desire for stagnation. The <b>Rejected (Denial)</b> are Shadows that take on the feeling of fear, the aversion towards others, ritualistic self-isolation and self-deprecation, the belief that one is unworthy. The <b>Indignant (Anger)</b> are Shadows that take on the feeling of anger and justice, the righteous hand, the desire to right wrongs and punish those that do not fall into what is right. The <b>Desperate (Bargaining) </b>are Shadows that take on the feeling of powerlessness, the victimization of others and the helplessness that plague them, the belief that there is no way to fight against fate or change oneself. The <b>Guilty (Guilt)</b> are Shadows that take on the feeling of responsibility, a perceived fault, the rejection of selfish thoughts mutated into the desire to give selflessly as to apologize or make amends. The <b>Worthless (Depression)</b> are Shadows that take on the feeling of imperfection, the overall wrongness of oneself and the exaggeration of faults. They mock the perception of importance and follow a sort of Nihilistic belief. The <b>Vainglorious (Acceptance)</b> are Shadows that take on the feeling of superiority, the acceptance of faults to a degree that implies perfection, the utter perversion of pride. </div> </div> </div>I feel like keeping this Axis, but shrinking it down to the basic five and expanding what they really are about.<br /> <br /> The Axis that is currently being reworked, I have yet to name; however, I find myself leaning towards <b><i>Loyalty </i></b>or <b><i>Dominion</i></b>. Basically, the Shadows originate in the feudal Labyrinth under the reign of the 8 (technically, 7) deceased <b>Guardians</b>. Since the <i>Ba Gua</i> has an associated element, organ, and animal, the Guardians were envisioned to be representations of these concepts.<br /> <br /> <i><u><b>ANOTHER ONE WHAT AN UPSET</b></u></i><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Horseman of the Sky</b><br /> Qian, Heaven, Force, Northwest, Strong, Creative, Head, Horse (The Horseman of the Sky), based on Shadows seeking to usurp humanity, worshiped by the Doppelgangers<br /> <i>{Death: Presumably to have died of natural causes}</i><br /> <br /> <b>The Pale Shepherd</b><br /> Dui, Lake, Open, West, Pleasure, Tranquil, Mouth, Goat (The Pale Shepherd), based on Shadows finding meaning in life, worshiped by the Eidolons<br /> <i>{Death: Poisoned, self-inflicted to escape The Horseman of the Sky-\u2019s systematic elimination of the other Guardians}</i><br /> <br /> <b>The Burning Oracle</b><br /> Li, Fire, Radiance, South, Dependence, Clarity, Eye, Pheasant (The Burning Oracle), based on Shadows understanding their nature, worshiped by the Voices<br /> <i>{Death: Burning, suicide in order to escape from The Horseman of the Sky}</i><br /> <br /> <b>The Infinite Serpent</b><br /> Zhen, Thunder, Shake, East, Movement, Initiative, Foot, Dragon (The Infinite Serpent), based on Shadows existing between the two forms, worshiped by the Phantasms<br /> <i>{Death: Dismemberment, died after being physically split in two by The Horseman of the Sky, the first major casualty in The Horseman\u2019s crusade}</i><br /> <br /> <b>The Cockatrice\u2019s Echo</b><br /> Xun, Wind, Ground, Southeast, Penetrating, Gentle, Thigh, Fowl (The Cockatrice\u2019s Echo), based on Shadows watching their Other Self, worshiped by the Exiles<br /> <i>{Death: Strangulation at the hands of the Guardian of the Graveyard}</i><br /> <br /> <b>The Legion of the Drowned</b><br /> Kan, Water, Gorge, North, Dangerous, In-Motion, Ear, Pig (The Legion of the Drowned), based on Shadows and the harvest of Gloom, worshiped by the Troglodytes<br /> <i>{Death: Drowning at the hands of the Guardian of the Graveyard}</i><br /> <br /> <b>The Guardian of the Graveyard</b><br /> Gen, Mountain, Bound, Northeast, Resting, Completion, Hand, Dog (The Guardian of the Graveyard), based on Shadows protecting the Labyrinth, worshiped by the Stalkers<br /> <i>{Death: Malnutrition due to the consumption of rotting and decaying food as well as the flesh of its former compatriots, forever loyal to The Horseman}</i><br /> <br /> <b>The Brood Mother</b><br /> Kun, Earth, Field, Southwest, Devoted, Receptive, Belly, Cow (The Brood Mother), based on Shadows and the Reflection, worshiped by the Progeny<br /> <i>{Death: Effectively still living, though entrapped within a crevice in the Labyrinth}</i> </div> </div> </div>The little &quot;worshiped by&quot; is meant to be what the Shadows would be considered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T15:33:51-08:00","id":370216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=370163#post370163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like the first PDF (That's ancient, ANCIENT news. The game has changed significantly). I scratched all of the artwork after that version and I've only just recently begun introducing images again (And admittedly the new ones need work too; they're really just there to break up walls of text). Trust me, you aren't the only person who had and has problems with the art. But I'm broke, and there's the whole matter of copyright when you go snatching images from the internet, so there aren't a whole lot of options.<br /> <br /> Thank you for clarifying the Wyrms. I'll abstain from peeking behind the curtain until you're ready to share with everybody; it's best not to poke around in the creative process until the gears are all in place, it can really muck up the works.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, good. I should really swing by that thread of yours sometime, see what's changed. And I know what you mean as far as art; just getting a bunch of generic images doesn't feel right. Luckily, we have a friend willing to draw us some really cool custom art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T14:53:33-07:00","id":607149,"title":"","content":"Long story short, the first idea I presented in this thread has changed quite a bit, though I think it's the better for it. Let me present...<br /> <br /> Viral: the Warped<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The disease in known by many names. Vitus Malus, the Twisting, Jigsaw, and many more by those few aware of it. It lurks in the shadows, spreading by tainted magic, the claws of strange, shadowy predators, and even the innocent touch of unknowing asymptomatics. Most who are infected die, the wrong part warped just the right way to be innocuously fatal. The majority of others are defiled, twisted into hateful, insane Things. The rest survive... in a fashion. Their flesh lives as it did before, even a bit better in fact, but the person who once lived in it is gone. Instead, a monster lives in their skin, a unnatural virus mutated into sapience. You are that Virus.*<br /> <br /> Virus: the Warped is a game of Alienation and Self-Control, as you wander through the world of the Host and attempt to define an identity from the ashes of a fallen life while struggling with a flesh that warps both with and without your whim.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Mood <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Alienation- Though everyone around you thinks otherwise, you are not human. You are a monster, an alien creature who cannot be truly human, though with much time and effort you may come close. In order to keep control, you must turn inward, keeping yourself under a leash in order to survive. In the end, you are alone, no matter how hard you try. You're the lonely man surrounded by friends, the silent screamer in a deaf crowd.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Theme<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Holding it together- It can be so easy to let go, to fail to maintain one's Coherency and become some Thing. The Warped must be cautious, for overuse of their greatest strengths will destroy them utterly. You have so little to gain, but so much to lose...</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> INHERENT AXIS<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Vector-How you infected your flesh and your natural inclinations.<br /> <br /> \u2022The Savage-Infection through beasts and other natural things.*<br /> <br /> \u2022The Tainted- Infection through defiled geometries, foul food, and other things made made wrong.<br /> <br /> \u2022The Given-Infection through blood, tears, and other thing of man.<br /> <br /> \u2022???-</div></div> </div> </div><br /> EXTERNAL AXIS <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Treatment-How you deal with your nature.<br /> \u2022&quot;The Humanists&quot;- Seek advantage through false humanity.<br /> <br /> \u2022&quot;The Prognosticators&quot;- Seek to understand the disease and other strange things of the shadows.*<br /> <br /> \u2022&quot;The Contained&quot;-Seek to master themselves and the world around them.<br /> \u2022???-</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Z-Axis<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Strains- Viruses joined by common traits, both of form and of self. May be &quot;born&quot; into or learned.<br /> EX:<br /> \u2022The McCarthy Syndrome- Memetic agents of discord.<br /> <br /> \u2022The Romero Plague- Death-Touched masters of undeath.<br /> <br /> \u2022The Techne Hubris- A Transhuman's nightmare, formed of a wicked mix of cell and circuit.*<br /> <br /> \u2022The Immunization Infection- Wound-mending guardians and farmers of the Host.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> SUPERNATURAL ADVANTAGE<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Morphism- How mutable and fluid their form is, and how in tune they are with their alien nature.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> FUEL<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> \u2022Misama-The energy of disease, born of that which infects.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> INTEGRITY STAT<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Coherency- How much the Warped controls their form, how easy it is to appear human, weakened by forsaking humanity or using Vicissitudes too often. At 0, result is Chimaera, also known as Things, who twist from second to second with feral violence.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> VIRTUE/VICE<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">\u2022Benignity- Positive influence, compulsion to stability and mankind.<br /> \u2022Malignancy- Negative influence, compulsion to mutation and monstrousness.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> POWERS<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Two sets of powers, one obvious and one not.<br /> \u2022Transmissions- The metaphysical side of the virus, subtle influences and minor gifts. Use is harmless to Virus.<br /> \u2022Vicissitudes- The physical side of the virus, blatant powers and potent mutations. Very obvious in use, and damages Coherency.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> MINOR TEMPLATE<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">\u2022Asymptomatics- Humans immune to the virus by some means. They are immune to the power of Transmissions, and may learn Transmissions that are used to try and affect them.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So, what do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T06:47:53-07:00","id":607805,"title":"","content":"One minor/major splat I've been working on for awhile is a group of True Immortals (Killing their body only pisses them off and their souls are Bound too Reality) that are free of Fate's Clutches.<br /> <br /> Fateless: the Pariah<br /> Theme: &quot;There are no strings on me&quot;<br /> Fate and other Beings direct Humanities path and most people never realize that they are little more then bit players in someone else's Story. Imagine how horrifying it must be too suddenly see that you are an extra on the stage of a play. Now Imagine the sheer terror that comes from being cast as the Victim or McGuffin for someone else to save or have as a motive to self improve. What would you do if you figured out how too remove yourself from the role cast for you and instead become one of the Audience or even one of the Stagehands.<br /> <br /> Mood: Despairing Dread/Dreadful Freedom<br /> Knowing that Fate cannot effect you is liberating, but it can also be something horrific. Time and the world move on, yet you cannot effect the course of the world anymore then a pebble in a river, you can cause ripples and change minor things but the river will still flow onwards, It takes the building of a Dam or many trenches too change it's course... Luckily you have Time.<br /> <br /> I've only got the basics of it currently since I've actually only recently Re-tolled it from what it was originally, I have got afew Terms for them though:<br /> <br /> Script: The type of story that Fate had Cast the Fateless in before they became what they are. (X-Splat/Internal Axis)<br /> School: The way/Philosophy of a Pariah after they have learned the basics of what they are (External/Social Splat)<br /> <br /> Catalyst: The initial reaction and cause of a Fateless to escape from the Role Fate Cast for them.<br /> <br /> Ennui: The Rating of how Bored a Fateless is with Life around them and their Role/Roles within the Narrative they make for themselves. (Integrity Equvilant, Both a Permanent and temporary Rating)<br /> <br /> Will be working on it abit more soon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T07:32:22-07:00","id":607886,"title":"","content":"<b>Viral</b>: I'm pretty interested in how different Warped relate to each other, and the themes of discovering and constructing identity inherent. I like that it's <i>internal</i> but <i>physical, </i>if that makes any sense. There should definitely be a focus on defining each Vector as different but similar diseases, like separate branches of the same evolutionary tree. There's room for a Z-splat, but maybe it should be Evolutions, or something. How you consciously changed your disease.<br /> <br /> <b>Fateless</b>: I'm not sure how much appeal there is in a game where the themes are &quot;you can't affect fate&quot; and &quot;immortality is boring.&quot; I like using Ennui as a stat, because it can actually push players toward doing things. Maybe since they're outside fate, they <i>can</i> change things? Or even if they can't affect it, they have extra insight into it? I do like the idea of becoming immortal by escaping fate.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've been kicking around an idea called <b>Controller</b>. The characters are all based around mind-control, but since I don't just want to make it Second Sight the fatsplat, they don't have any other &quot;psychic powers.&quot; The fuel stat is Focus, and instead of spending it you move it around. How much Focus you have allocated to a person/body determines how much control you have over them, but if you move too much away from your body you risk losing it. Since I'm restricting how &quot;psychic&quot; they can be* I'm having trouble coming up with powers beyond the core stuff. I've got some, but it doesn't feel like a gameline's worth.<br /> <br /> *the rule I keep telling myself is &quot;no telekinesis,&quot; which is just basically a reminder to stay away from stuff like setting people on fire, flying, seeing ghosts, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T08:39:33-07:00","id":607930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=607886#post607886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Fateless</b>: I'm not sure how much appeal there is in a game where the themes are &quot;you can't affect fate&quot; and &quot;immortality is boring.&quot; I like using Ennui as a stat, because it can actually push players toward doing things. Maybe since they're outside fate, they <i>can</i> change things? Or even if they can't affect it, they have extra insight into it? I do like the idea of becoming immortal by escaping fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can see Fates Stings and Prompts, and can slightly avert/divert them. Part of the Horror i want too put in peoples hands is... &quot;So you can See whats going too happen but if you do anything to change it Fate will just go around you and do it anyway&quot; Think.. Final Destination. (The First one, not the Sequels) you can see and change things a little But SOMEONE Needs to die too act as someone else's Plot Token/Motivator. (Depending on the Story Fate is telling ofcourse)<br /> <br /> They also have the Ability to &quot;Change&quot; the Narrative of a story for a short period and make the end result slightly different then it would be, nothing like giving a Happy ending too someone Who's Fate is too be Murdered, but maybe make it so they are viscously attacked and Survive (Think changing a Film's Rating from R to Pg)<br /> <br /> The Idea I was playing with is the 3 Social splats, each of them has a Different &quot;Special&quot; ability they can do which effects Fate in a different way. Although it might be better to have them as a Legacy/Bloodline/etc thing for them... Anyway the Idea's are<br /> <br /> &quot;Showstoppers&quot;/Smashers: They Don't like the Play, and take it out on the Stage and the Actors. They Can Take an Active Fate/Plan from Fate and Destroy any one Element of it, Stopping it from working how it would normally.<br /> <br /> &quot;Stagehands&quot;/Assistants: They see themselves as being Tasked with Assisting Fate with it's Plays, but Softening them for a More Humane touch, lessening the Blow with changing the Cast and letting themselves take the place of some of the others that would be effected. At the Highest they can Craft a New Fate for someone aslong as they take that place for themselves.<br /> <br /> &quot;Directors&quot;/Control Freaks: Having been cast as a Victim or Monster/Bully within a Story, you can't help but fancy your hand at making a better Story then Fate Can, Taking the Role of the Director of a Film you use your Knowledge too whisper and Manipulate Fate into how you want it. With your Knowledge of Fate you can play with the Fate that is in Effect currently and totally re-write it, but like A Film having different Directors taking control of it, sometimes people Notice.<br /> <br /> I Also have an Adversary for them aswell. No Minor Splat for them yet though (Still toying with if they should be considered a Minor/Major Splat themselves. Also They Do not Register as Kin for Beasts.. nor do their Adversaries.<br /> <br /> Antagonist: Unborn; They are the physical and spiritual embodiments of Fate's plan and it's possible Futures Denied. They Cannot Exist normally but sometimes when a Fateless makes a play at Fate and causes disasterous effects (Dramatic Failures on a Major Fate Effect) they can be brought into being, they by simply being Causes Fate and the Barriers between worlds too fade, leaving behind destroyed lives, Ghosts and other Monsterous creations that shouldn't exist (And Rapidly Die if they don't Feast on other Peoples Fates causing them too become a Husk) If not stopped quickly or the Effect that created it averted/repaired they can and will become something new and Inch the World closer too it's destruction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":3981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","user":"RickmanUK","date":"07-30-2015, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T10:02:03-07:00","id":608069,"title":"","content":"This seems like a good place to mention that Xallace and I have continued development on Dragon: the Inheritance, with the help of some of the folks on GitP. We've made a lot of progress on the Legacies and setting information, including every single Auxiliary that a starting character has access to. We've also made a fair number of revisions to existing abilities, antagonists, and other things. As soon as a slot opens up in our group's playing time, we'll be starting playtesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T10:06:41-07:00","id":615256,"title":"","content":"Posted the Intro Chapter for my Pariahs over <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/615238-fateless-the-pariah\">Here</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T12:05:56-07:00","id":615425,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, I should also mention that our <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1h-o7bWocPX_6vO9PCfVYcCyApJMTudFcZGUCOmjw1Ok/\" target=\"_blank\">doc</a> is available for viewing now. I made a dedicated thread for it a while back, but only a couple people posted in it, so I think it slipped by a few of the people who were interested here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T13:07:51-07:00","id":615495,"title":"","content":"After playing <i>way</i> too much Majora's Mask, it inspired me/maddened me.<br /> <br /> <b>Shaman: the Masked</b><br /> Since ancient times, masks have held a certain power. They hide your identity, free your inhibitions, they assuage your fear. In many cultures, masks hold even greater power: speaking to animals and the dead, commanding the forces of nature, and preserving the memories of ancestors.<br /> <br /> <b>Mood:</b> Reverence for Nature: The powers of the Shaman are not their own, coming from forces that they don't understand. As a result, they must tread cautiously.<br /> <br /> <b>Theme:</b> Becoming the Mask; Those who constantly wear masks must be careful that they don't lose themselves. This is especially true when the mask you're wearing is overflowing with supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> <b>Inherent Axis:</b> Sympathy; the part of the World Soul that called out to you in the first place. Determines what type of powers your first Mask is allowed to have, as well as what kinds of Masks you can most easily make.<br /> <br /> <b>Social Axis:</b> Tradition; The cultural tradition your Masks descend from. You don't necessarily have to <i>come</i> from that culture, but you have to honestly and seriously draw inspiration from it, although putting an unusual twist on it is common in modern times.<br /> <br /> <b>Power Stat:</b> Instead of a singular Power Stat, Masquers have two stats: Animus, and the Power of their Masks, each of which is capped at 5. Animus represents the Shaman's connection to the World Soul, and how strongly their will is attuned to it. A Mask's Power represents the potency and variety of effects it can achieve.<br /> <br /> <b>Fuel:</b> Noctis; The energy of the World Soul, Noctis is found in all places, but can only be harnessed in certain by those sensitive to the World Soul, such as Shamans.<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> Detachment; Instead of a singular Integrity stat, each Mask has its own level of Detachment, representing how separate the Shaman is from the persona of the Mask. Low Detachment causes a Mask's Compulsions to remain for longer, but it also makes using that Mask's power easier. Conversely, a high Detachment allows you to more easily resist a Mask's Compulsion, but makes its powers less reliable.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue/Vice:</b> The character retains their normal Virtue and Vice, but each Mask has its own Compulsion, which acts similarly. Each Compulsion is unique to the Mask, and can offer both Noctis and Willpower when acted upon.<br /> <br /> <b>Powers:</b> The powers of the Shaman come from their Masks. Each Mask falls under one of X loose groupings, which determines what type of powers available to it. Mechanically, the powers of Masks are rather narrow, being attuned to a specific subset of the wider category they fall in, but their level of control is relatively high as a result.<ul><li>Beast: Masks of Beasts allow communication and influence over their subjects. (Panthers, Dogs, Sharks)</li> <li>Celestial: The stars and planets help to weave fate on your behalf. (Mars as Warrior, Sirius for Wealth)</li> <li>Dream: The most direct connection to the World Soul, these masks touch a part of the Astral. (Entering an Oneros, evoking emotions, warding off nightmares)</li> <li>Elements: The elements of nature heed the call of Masks of Elements. (Smoke, Winds, Thunder)</li> <li>Funeral: Funeral Masks commemorate the dead and call upon ghosts. (using the skills of a dead ancestor, repelling evil ghosts)</li> </ul><b>Minor Template:</b> Dreamwalkers; Individuals who are innately connected to the World Soul, but without the ability to form that connection into a Mask. They have difficulty keeping themselves distinct from their internalized &quot;Mask&quot;, but they have an intuitive control over their powers.<br /> <br /> I'll probably start work on it later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T17:09:53-07:00","id":615765,"title":"","content":"Succubi: The Desire<br /> <br /> The Bi, are short for Succubi/Incubi.<br /> <br /> The Bi are wet dreams, sexual fantasies that so hungered to be real, that they found away to cross the barrier between desire and reality.<br /> <br /> A Bi starts off as a simple wet dream that in the face of they're Dreamer's strong sexual desires, becomes self aware.<br /> <br /> To be born in the world the Bi needs a physical body, and so the Bi begs his/her Dreamer to help, to offer up someone as scarifice so that they can be made real.<br /> <br /> It has to be someone the Dreamer loves or who loves the Dreamer.<br /> <br /> Once offered, piece by piece that loved ones place in reality starts disappearing. At first people simple forget they're names, then records disappear, Birth Certificates, Gym Memberships,even criminal records.<br /> <br /> Then people the loved one know they're whole lives began see them as strangers, history seems to rewrite itself, removing they're presence from itself, until they just disappear, banished to the dreams and nightmarea of those who they once knew, trapped forever unless they merge with someones sexual fantasy to become one of the Bi themselves, although by that point even they have forgotten who they were.<br /> <br /> The Bi one the other hand becomes more real, first as an emphreal phantom only thier Dreamers can see, then something others can see out of the corner of they're eyes, becaming more physically real till reality rewrites history, making a place for them, based on the Dreamers' fantasies.<br /> <br /> Maybe one Dreamer's dreams of a tough, but sexy vice cop, who upon becoming real finds that she has a history with the NYPD, one that has never actually occurred.<br /> <br /> Still, the transition to real is an unnatural one, it needs to be sustained, so the Bi mantains his/her place in reality, by drawning on the sexual energies of her Dreamer. This causes the Dreamers health deteriate, so the Bi seeks out others to feed her need for sexual energy.<br /> <br /> Themes: Obsessions, Dark Dreams, the boarder between what's real and what's not. The Bi (short for Succubi/Incubi) are basically dark, dangerous erotic Tulpas sort of, whose very existance has a dark price to pay).<br /> <br /> Inheriant Splats<br /> <br /> Lilitu- Born from fantasies where the dreamer is dominated.<br /> <br /> Lamia- Born from sexual fantasies invovling death or undeath.<br /> <br /> Yakshi- Born from dreams where the Dreamer sexually dominates the Bi.<br /> <br /> Qarinah- Born from Dreams of sexual encounters with none humaniod creatures.<br /> <br /> Rusalaka- Born from Romantic Dreams.<br /> <br /> Mara- Born from erotic dreams invovling rage, hate, personal torment.<br /> <br /> Out Splats: The Drives, the Drives are what pushes the Bi to survive beyond mere existance.<br /> <br /> Love: A Bi who is Driven by love, has usually, but not always fallen in love with the Dreamer.<br /> <br /> Curisosity: They wanted to know what the real world was like, and seek to explore it.<br /> <br /> Fear: There something in the Dreamer's dreams with them, something that shouldn't have been in there and it scared them.<br /> <br /> Loneliness- They found it Lonely in the dreams, they wanted company beyond the Dreamer.<br /> <br /> Hedonism: The real world is filled pleasures for all the senses, and the Bi with this drive want to experience them all.<br /> <br /> Anatogonist Drives: Revenge, those Bi who are Driven by the need to seek revenge against thier Dreamer or Dreamers in general, the Guilty, who feed horrible about the person who was destroyed for thier freedom, the Guilty are devoted to saving their victim no matter the cost to herself or her own kind, very self hating.<br /> <br /> Power Stat: Dreamer, the greater they're mystical connection to they're Dreamer and his/her desires/sexual fantasies, the more powerful the Bi's magic. A Bi who feeds on her Dreamer too often can drain too much life force, making her Dreamer Points drop tempororily until her Dreamer, heals all lethal damage. Within 20 feet of her Dreamer, her Dreamer stat counts as double its actual number.<br /> <br /> Fuel Stat: Orgasms: The mystical engery from a mortal or none Bi Supernatural beings orgasm, is used to keep unreality at bay and to fuel his/her magic. A Bi has to expend a point of Orgasm per day to keep her place in reality from eroding.<br /> <br /> Intergity Stat: Reality: The higher Reality is, the more real the Bi is, the lower, the less real the Bi is. A Bi with a Reality of 10, needs only spend 1 Orgasm per week to keep her Reality from eroding, a Bi at Reality 1, is empheral in twilight when not with 5 miles of her Dreamer.<br /> <br /> Powers: Escstacies<br /> <br /> Example Escstacy, Speak with nightmares. The Bi speaks in unknowable tongue and her target's nightmares answer back, telling her of the targets fears. Dreamer + Empathy vs. Compsure + Supernatural Stat.<br /> <br /> Killer Orgasm- Its starts of as pleasant sensation in the groin, spreads out in waves throughout the body, before muscles contractions start, pleasant at first, then growing painful as they get stronger, eventual ripping muscles aparts, and breaking bone, turning they're insides into a. bloody pulp, but leaving they're external flesh unharmed, leaving them with a deranged smile on their dead face. Dreamer + Strength vs. Stamina + Supernal Trait.<br /> <br /> The Little death, spend a point of orgasm, and the Bi can take on the appearance of a Corpse or some type of undead. It can fool both the senses and Supernatural detection. Roll Dreamer + Sublefuge vs. Resolve + Supernatural Stat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 08-04-2015, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T16:57:00-07:00","id":623757,"title":"","content":"<b>Shaman</b>: I can see the Majora's Mask influence, certainly. I'd assume that those who bottom out on Detachment would serve as the antagonists? And what's your justification for a Shaman no longer having any sort of mortal Integrity? Why don't they care about the sorts of things that people do, anymore? They certainly can't wear a mask all the time, no matter how much they might wish to.<br /> <br /> <b>Succubi</b>: Firstly, I'd change the headliner to be <i>Succubus</i>, as WoD Splat titles are always singular of the represented race. As risqu\u00e9 and controversial (even down to being among a player group) as the splat is, I can actually see some merit in your idea. It's certainly not someone somebody else has tried, though it may be an option to have the Dreamer be the protagonist, him/herself being mortal and the Bi (or indeed, other demon, should we represent other ideas) being either GM-controlled based on the Dreamer's actions or controlled by a PC, either the same as or different to the one controlling the Dreamer.<br /> <br /> Perhaps you could consider expanding the idea to include other sorts of Demons? And I'd like to note that the sort of person that would sacrifice a loved one to bring a dream to live is probably pretty morally bankrupt, or at least has some sort of problem.<br /> <br /> <i>@One Tin Soldier</i>: I took a flip through <i>Inheritance</i> before I created my account, and you have some solid ideas. I'll take a look at the new additions when I have a spare moment and let you know what I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6393-chuckles","name":"Chuckles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T19:17:22-07:00","id":623873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chuckles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=623757#post623757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Shaman</b>: I can see the Majora's Mask influence, certainly. I'd assume that those who bottom out on Detachment would serve as the antagonists? And what's your justification for a Shaman no longer having any sort of mortal Integrity? Why don't they care about the sorts of things that people do, anymore? They certainly can't wear a mask all the time, no matter how much they might wish to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, it was more of a mechanical decision than anything else. I suppose having Integrity in addition to Detachment wouldn't be <i>too</i> taxing, but I was worried that having both might be more annoying than anything. Andthen there's the question of whether a breaking point might apply to Integrity, Detachment, or both, and how to adjudicate that.<br /> <br /> Another thing I'm having trouble with is how to run the actual mechanics of the mask, because I want each mask to be unique enough that players feel like it's <i>their</i> mask, but I also want to have it be as mechanically simple and concise as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 08-11-2015, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T19:59:45-07:00","id":623889,"title":"","content":"Perhaps a base Integrity equivalent (Identity? Something related to sense of self) related to the Shaman, while each Mask has it's own Identity? When the Mask's identity grows greater than the Shaman's, then you start having problems with the Mask taking over? It's certainly something we can work with and make things interesting.<br /> <br /> As for the Masks, maybe look at stuff like Genius' wonders and the ideas used to make them for ideas on the mechanics to make them. Players can easily develop their own concepts for the Masks.<br /> <br /> And I forgot to suggest; perhaps a sort of Mask related to increasing physical ability and skill? Various images are represented, but I keep thinking &quot;Fierce Deity Link&quot; and even &quot;Hollows/Visored.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or maybe physical power comes with taking on the Identity of a Mask, surrendering parts of yourself to the Identity of the thing within for the sake of power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6393-chuckles","name":"Chuckles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T21:19:38-07:00","id":623913,"title":"","content":"I have, at one point, totally wanted to hash out Geist, Beast, and Demon into a Lovecraft-inspired post apocalypse setting that is probably more &quot;Shin Megami Tensei meets MASK&quot; than I was looking to do at the outset - players are &quot;ronin,&quot; young adults who live in &quot;the Zone,&quot; a sort of apocalyptic landscape created by breaking down the barriers between the real world and the Dreamlands, and they've all got cyberware that lets them use little cards that burn out instead of their own sanity when using magic stolen from the elder beings who wander the landscape under the employ of a mad scientist turned megalomaniac. The general theme was to let horror come from the sorts of things you'd allow yourself to do and think when you're just trying to survive. Also, that to even use the technology reserved for interacting with the monsters, you have to face your own inadequacies and shortcomings and come out on top. Not sure how I'd enforce that with the rules, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T12:03:38-07:00","id":624535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chuckles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=623889#post623889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps a base Integrity equivalent (Identity? Something related to sense of self) related to the Shaman, while each Mask has it's own Identity? When the Mask's identity grows greater than the Shaman's, then you start having problems with the Mask taking over? It's certainly something we can work with and make things interesting.<br /> <br /> As for the Masks, maybe look at stuff like Genius' wonders and the ideas used to make them for ideas on the mechanics to make them. Players can easily develop their own concepts for the Masks.<br /> <br /> And I forgot to suggest; perhaps a sort of Mask related to increasing physical ability and skill? Various images are represented, but I keep thinking &quot;Fierce Deity Link&quot; and even &quot;Hollows/Visored.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or maybe physical power comes with taking on the Identity of a Mask, surrendering parts of yourself to the Identity of the thing within for the sake of power?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that may work. I was thinking that physical power could be one of the effects built into the mask itself (so a Cheetah mask might exist to improve speed, an Earth-based mask might grant armor or raise Stamina, etc.). You take on the persona of the mask immediately upon wearing it. Each mask has a Compulsion, which acts like Mask/Dirge or Blood/Bone for Vamps and Wolves, where acting on it refills Willpower and Fuel, but can cause a breaking point. So if you were wearing a Wolf mask, you might have &quot;Asserting Dominance&quot; as a Compulsion. Putting somebody down would offer 1 willpower and 1 fuel, while killing a rival would offer a full refill and a large amount of fuel, but if that's outside the character's normal personality, then they suffer a breaking point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T18:41:27-07:00","id":624922,"title":"","content":"Sounds good, try working with the model. Another thing I wanted to question you on; what's the endgame of a Shaman? What's the apex of power they aspire to, and what of the things that they become when they lose themselves fully?<br /> <br /> By the way, you may want to discuss the different sizes and shapes of a mask. Because they range from anything like domino-mask sized to being <i>huge</i>, let alone the different aesthetics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6393-chuckles","name":"Chuckles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T18:55:01-07:00","id":624926,"title":"","content":"<b>Giant: the Unhallowed</b><br /> There were giants, once, but now they're all gone -- their corpses decomposed into the Firmament that composed them, which became part of the hills, graveyards, corpses and everything else a la the way everything in the universe is made up of everything else. &quot;Giants' graves,&quot; where the giant actually died, are saturated with Firmament, so that the land remembers when it was a living creature; occasionally, when a mortal resonates enough with the giant buried in a grave, the Firmament in them remembers when it was a giant and grants them dominion and authority. This process isn't quite a transformation of a mortal into a giant so much as a reincarnation of the giant -- it's not quite Jolene, any more; it's the giant buried in the grave, incarnated with Jolene's personality and memories, although her connection to these is slowly ablated away as the endless history of the giant replaces her own brief mayfly life.<br /> <br /> A giant is capable of reminding the Firmament in everything that it was once part of them, awakening stones, mortals and laws to act as their limbs. It's not enough, though, to be able to remember the past -- when a giant inhales Firmament, they build up their fragile, temporal, mortal body into a colossus, a smaller manifestation of their predecessors and their ancient heritage. The problem with this, of course, is that all the giants are dead. A giant who resembles a mortal gets some allowances from Time, but when they assume their mighty antediluvian Stature, reality begins to ablate it away, removing them from human perceptions first before slowly fossilizing them and turning them to dust. By saturating an environment with their Firmament, a giant can claim it, making it their own<br /> <br /> <b>X-Axis</b>: Primogeniture -- there are many lineages of giants, but based on the circumstances of their graves and the values of their children, many can be divided thus:<br /> <b><i>Asuras</i></b>, giants who were buried amongst and embody death and war; they command fealty from the deceased and slaughter and consume that which would endanger their houses.<br /> <b><i>Fomorians</i></b>, giants who were buried in and embody liminal places; prophets, storytellers and historians, they know that time is cyclical and thus remember what they will see.<br /> <b><i>Jotunn</i></b>, giants who were buried in and embody chaos and the wild; with rain for blood and ice in their eyes, they can survive outside the borders of the civilized like none other.<br /> <b><i>Nephilim</i></b>, giants who were buried in and embody sites of creation; as the children of angels, the Nephilim build up religions, monuments and towers as extensions of themselves.<br /> <b><i>Uranians</i></b>, giants who were buried in and embody temples and palaces of mastery; there is a divine order which each recognizes, and they train themselves, and everything, to obey.<br /> <br /> <b>Y-Axis</b>: Legacy -- while most giants have a hand in temporal power structures, certain schools of thought regarding breaking the chain of succession have persisted.<br /> <b>Gold</b>: Hierophants of the Golden Legacy venerate and seek out their original selves, in the hopes that some means of escaping the vicious cycle exists. Many form multi-generational religions that worship the Colossi, giants who have persisted long enough that they can no longer exist inside the flow of time, as living records of the past.<br /> <b>Silver</b>: Sages of the Silver Legacy seek to amass knowledge and pass it on to their successors, considering the memory loss between deaths to be the primary problem with gigantism; by preserving their knowledge and transplanting their own memories into artifacts of Firmament, they seek immortality through their descendants.<br /> <b>Bronze</b>: Fisher-Kings of the Bronze Legacy seek peace through conquest. By establishing little kingdoms of their own, in accumulated power and land that can be attended and gardened, they seek to satisfy the constant dominance drive infused in them by their long-dead ancestors -- and, maybe, create worlds where Time can't hunt them down.<br /> <b>Iron</b>: Demiurges of the Iron Legacy transform themselves. Immortality is nice, but having your personality slowly eclipsed by a long-dead terror and reincarnating through human bodies makes gigantism far worse than is acceptable; the Demiurges forge Firmament to take different forms, ones that can survive a world trying constantly to kill them.<br /> <br /> <b>Theme</b>: Sins of the Fathers. A giant is an inheritor of a legacy dating back to the beginning of the universe; the continuity of a giant's psyche over multiple descendants means that long-lived rivals may eliminate you for something you did in a past incarnation, as a person you can no longer recall being. Breaking from the chain of succession is death. Think of it as inheriting an estate from your grandfather -- and finding evidence of deep debt to the Russian mob in the basement. You could become incompetent and die young, or you could assume the mantle of power and responsibility and desperation... and someday wind up the dead old man who wills his estate and power to a fresh-faced stranger.<br /> <br /> <b>Power</b>: Testament, the degree to which the giant's &quot;will&quot; is enacted through her descendant.<br /> <br /> <b>Fuel</b>: Firmament -- measuring the amount of &quot;free&quot; Firmament the giant has inside, to be shaped into the half-literal, half-metaphysical body of a titan.<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity</b>: Vitality -- a giant's psychology demands that they take control, rather than surrender to outside forces; those who fail to act begin to stagnate, eventually decaying or fossilizing unless they take steps to reclaim control.<br /> <br /> <b>Powers</b>: <i>Remembrances</i>, ways the giant forces her Firmament to remember when it was part of someone or something else. A mortal whose Firmament is awakened obeys the giant as a father; stone may remember being sand, or metal slag and ore, and the dead, who are all memories, may be changed and restored.<br /> <i>Claims</i>, places and objects saturated with Firmament and made the property of a giant; the land and the king are one, and so a giant exercises divine right over all her Claims, mastering them and knowing them as herself.<br /> <i>Stature,</i> the last-ditch weapon; a giant who swallows Firmament in mass quantities, allowing it to redesign her body, gains the strength and magical mettle of her predecessors, but exposes herself to the ravages of Time in doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T16:28:19-07:00","id":626040,"title":"","content":"Cool concept, Keter. Do you have an antagonist in mind? Or do you intend the physical conflict to just be between the Giants themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6393-chuckles","name":"Chuckles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T17:03:46-07:00","id":626063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chuckles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=626040#post626040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool concept, Keter. Do you have an antagonist in mind? Or do you intend the physical conflict to just be between the Giants themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most conflict, I figured, would be between giants -- there's a general understanding in their society that the next person to inherit a giant's spirit is that giant, and thus there are a hell of a lot of long-standing grudges that Butterfly Effected out over time. Also, two giants can't Claim the same place at the same time, which should provoke squabbles and politics. The Colossi are especially guilty of this -- with long memories and deep pockets, they can make a giant's life a living hell, and they actually need Claims to exist, as they're incapable of staying in the real world without fossilizing and burning away.<br /> <br /> As for external threats, I've considered the &quot;Theoi,&quot; or &quot;New Gods&quot; -- the deities of Mt. Olympus, Asgard and various other pantheons, the ones worshipped by humans, those deities who brought the flood and slew the giants. They lack Firmament in their bodies, divorced entirely from the raw earth of giants, and either claim or are claimed to be the ones who originally slaughtered the giants in the Titanomachy; if a giant is someone who inherited a mansion hiding an ancient mystery from her deceased uncle, the Theoi are the hitmen who come to the door, knock her out and burn the mansion down with the mystery unsolved, because &quot;it is better that you never find out.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T18:37:10-07:00","id":626128,"title":"","content":"Reminds me of the American Gods, except the old gods in Gaiman's book are the new gods here. Definitely an interesting idea to play with.<br /> <br /> So I'm guessing that Testament is also a measure of how the mortal identity is being subsumed by that of the giant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6393-chuckles","name":"Chuckles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T19:49:10-07:00","id":626154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chuckles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=626128#post626128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reminds me of the American Gods, except the old gods in Gaiman's book are the new gods here. Definitely an interesting idea to play with.<br /> <br /> So I'm guessing that Testament is also a measure of how the mortal identity is being subsumed by that of the giant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. As Testament increases, the giant becomes increasingly detached from her mortal identity -- it becomes less something in which she lives and to which she has emotional connections, and more a weird ritual she enacts to honor the person who used to occupy the body. While the mortal identity can be retained with effort, once a giant reaches the age and degree of transformation necessary to be considered a Colossus, it's likely that the person she was is just a thin veneer on the body of an eternal, silent monolith-god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T20:01:54-07:00","id":626186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=626154#post626154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep. As Testament increases, the giant becomes increasingly detached from her mortal identity -- it becomes less something in which she lives and to which she has emotional connections, and more a weird ritual she enacts to honor the person who used to occupy the body. While the mortal identity can be retained with effort, once a giant reaches the age and degree of transformation necessary to be considered a Colossus, it's likely that the person she was is just a thin veneer on the body of an eternal, silent monolith-god.</div> </div> </div> </div> Of course, a Demiurge might have something to say about that...<br /> <br /> Anyway, I really like this idea you've had here. Great work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T10:46:28-07:00","id":626737,"title":"","content":"Really interesting, it deserves to be worked and expanded.<br /> <br /> But I think the Theoi needs a better examination. With every Giant knowing what it is to be indebted without knowing, because of a previous life, I don't think most of them would stick to this idea of fighting one another over dead grudges. Unless they are forced to.<br /> <br /> Also, something have to link them together both to stir the necessity of a society and to justify the formation of groups of giants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T19:13:11-07:00","id":630562,"title":"","content":"Part of it is that, as giants become stronger -- both personally and in terms of political power -- their original personalities become closer and closer to those of their primogenitors, who <i>do </i>believe, in general, that dead grudges matter. The basic concept is an old boys' club -- giant society is controlled by your elders and parents; by the time someone on the bottom has reached the top, they've become the exact same kind of person.<br /> <br /> (Of course, there's also general, all-purpose political infighting, and a concept I'm working on, a giant's &quot;Bequests&quot; -- political organizations, buildings and important possessions marked by a giant's former incarnations. A giant who awakens doesn't necessarily awaken alone -- many will have Merits representing their Bequests, sources of support, aides, retainers and servitors created by their past incarnations. A &quot;Crown&quot; can be set up to supply certain supernatural benefits to mortals, as long as they faithfully serve the will of the giant who created it -- many use Crowns to create sources of wealth and power for their descendants, and, at the same time, act as strong influences, with apparent authority and wisdom, on confused new giants. Often, giants whose ancestors collaborated are given Bequests that draw them together. Ultimately, I see giant society as being very much about lines of inheritance and influence -- you can trust Smith because his father and your father worked together, although of course you can't trust him *too* much because his father and your father were in a <i>tenuous business alliance </i>and those tend to fall through.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T13:32:28-07:00","id":631493,"title":"","content":"Hero: The Exiled<br /> A game inspired by exotic expatriates in superhero stories, science fiction, and fantasy. Wonder Woman, Superman, Stitch, Hellboy, and so on.<br /> You're living in a huge, sophisticated culture, 4,000 years after the discovery of magic, and 2,000 years after that weird guy was born in Nazarath. You're a loyal subject of either the Egyptian Pharaoh, the Assyrian Emperor, the Queens of Minoa, or the Xia Emperor. I suppose you could be a filthy barbarian too.<br /> You've used magic to enhance your body to the peak of human perfection, or to mimic the abilities of animals, or even to become a machine, transcending the limits of biology.<br /> You've travelled to an exotic, primitive dimension. Maybe you were forced there against your will, flung there accidentally, or wanted to explore the ultimate undiscovered country.<br /> The problem is that the new dimension doesn't have magic, and dimensional travel is magic. You're stuck there permanently, with no magical powers. It's a good thing some of your enhancements still work. You'll need them to survive... in the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1430-gareth3","name":"Gareth3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T02:30:34-07:00","id":632102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gareth3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=631493#post631493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hero: The Exiled<br /> A game inspired by exotic expatriates in superhero stories, science fiction, and fantasy. Wonder Woman, Superman, Stitch, Hellboy, and so on.<br /> You're living in a huge, sophisticated culture, 4,000 years after the discovery of magic, and 2,000 years after that weird guy was born in Nazarath. You're a loyal subject of either the Egyptian Pharaoh, the Assyrian Emperor, the Queens of Minoa, or the Xia Emperor. I suppose you could be a filthy barbarian too.<br /> You've used magic to enhance your body to the peak of human perfection, or to mimic the abilities of animals, or even to become a machine, transcending the limits of biology.<br /> You've travelled to an exotic, primitive dimension. Maybe you were forced there against your will, flung there accidentally, or wanted to explore the ultimate undiscovered country.<br /> The problem is that the new dimension doesn't have magic, and dimensional travel is magic. You're stuck there permanently, with no magical powers. It's a good thing some of your enhancements still work. You'll need them to survive... in the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes me think of a Campaign i ran.... With an Exalted in the OWoD..... Solar's are literally Vampire Killers by using ANY of their powers.... That and Drinking from a Solar was Like Drinking the Sun....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T14:04:39-07:00","id":632707,"title":"","content":"You could make it more challenging by not allowing the Solar to use Charms in the WOD. He has to get by on superior stats alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1430-gareth3","name":"Gareth3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T07:50:59-07:00","id":650108,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So, this is what came up in a different thread, but I\u2019ve heavily added and brainstormed the topic on this board since then. Monarch is a game where you play an alien bug monster queen human hybrid in charge of your own little &quot;Hive&quot;. </span></span> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Monarchs as they are called are a fusion of alien and human life that exist to inessence act as the intermediaries of a vast, but fragmented Hive Mind. Most Monarchs were originally humans exposed to a virus that infected them and twisted their bodies. Most lose their will and completely degenerate, but a lucky few evolve all to better the greater whole that is the Swarm. Their free will is left to them entirely at this point and they are thrust into a position of potentially great power. However, choosing to go against the Hive as a whole practically means death. If you would not serve, you are easily replaced.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Swarm, collectively can be best described as an interdimensional race that take resemble a mix of bugs, reptiles, and dinosaurs, mixed with odd traits such as resembling shadows and metal. Most are barely the more than animals, but in a way they don\u2019t need to be too smart as they are controlled by the Monarchs, the Agents of the Hive Mind\u2019s fractured will.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While it is known that the Swarm possesses its own world or perhaps even worlds, Earth\u2019s environment seems to actively reject the Swarm\u2019s presence, in effect killing them. Monarchs, being meldings of native and alien, are able to survive on Earth unaided. Although, one wonders why go to the trouble of going through Earth in the first place since logically, there should be other, less hazardous worlds to visit. The Monarchs certainly don\u2019t know.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Key Powers</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Monarchs are able to shift from human form into a form more fitting to the Swarm\u2019s needs. When the Monarch assumes her \u201cLord\u201d form, she is able to use her access to studies to the best of her abilities at the cost of horrific transformation into an inhuman creature. Otherwise, Monarchs are perfectly indistinguishable from normal humans\u2026 and just about as capable. Without assuming a Swarm form, they lack access to the majority of their powers. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As a further limitation, a Monarch\u2019s powers require that she invests her Authority to keep them active. While Authority is more of a pool rather than a \u201cfuel\u201d trait, this limitation often prevents the Monarch from using herself or her swarm to their fullest. Authority must be divided up evenly between the Monarch and her servants.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All Monarchs possess a small degree of telepathy. Specifically, the ability to send messages at Will, but for the most part this has a few weaknesses. First, outside of her own Broods, a Monarch\u2019s innate telepathy is rather short range and by default only other Monarchs and telepaths can interpret it. On top of that it is also \u201cunsecured\u201d allowing any telepath within range to catch wind of it, in particular other monarchs. Thankfully, \u201cin-Brood\u201d telepathy has an effective range of 1 Mile, allowing the Monarch to command her Brood from range.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All Monarchs possess the ability to create a Hive Cluster or Domain. Essentially, it is a pocket dimension where the the Monarch may create her forces on Earth. While Earth\u2019s environment is hazardous to the Swarm, a Hive Cluster is \u201cxenoformed\u201d enough to allow the Swarm\u2019s creatures to exist unaided. Though the Hive Cluster is a pocket dimension, it does have one weakness and liability: Hive Clusters require a physical gateway within real space to access it, such as either a pit or doorway. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Monarchs may Create Broods within their domains, essentially, part cult, part\u2026 swarm. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One unique feature of Monarchs is their ability to create special \u201cretainers\u201d for themselves either by \u201cbirthing\u201d specialized minions or by converting an existing humans to the fold. In either case, the Monarch imbues a small portion of her own powers onto the new \u201cHeralds\u201d.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">However, as Earth\u2019s environment literally sears away any Swarm creature caught within it, a Monarch\u2019s agents cannot act within the normal or even the magical worlds connected to the world\u2026 at least, not without the Monarch\u2019s investment. By investing a portion of her own will directly into her Swarm, the Monarch grants limited protection from the environment to her agents, preventing them from perish just by breathing. However, this protection is limited. So long as the Monarch can keep channeling, her agents are protected, once her Authority is removed, her agents rapidly turn into vapor as even their remains break down. This limitation is what keeps the Swarm from growing out of control, as even will full Authority invested, the swarm will never be large enough to wipe out a city or even a town all by itself.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Themes:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You are in charge: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Monarchs all rule over their own little Hives, effectively making the Kings and Queens of their personal domains. They however have to handle the political issues that come with that such as controlling their Swarm.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Castes:</b> Representation of the intended original purpose of the Hivemind behind a Monarch\u2019s \u201crebirth\u201d.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Warrior- Born to fight and kill, either for offense or defense of the Hive. Focus on combat, warfare, conquest, though not necessarily overt.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tender- Created to maintain the conditions and health of the hive. Primary directive is support, recovery, resource management. Can be rather brutal if defense is needed. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scribe- Made for thinking, exploration, crate work. Strength comes from knowledge and obtaining it is necessary. Experimentation and exploration are the primary focuses. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Envoy- Exists to coerce and coordinate other Monarchs together, and on Earth, to allow for diplomacy. Also acts as the primary interpreters of the Hive Mind\u2019s Will.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Ideology.</b> In essence, as rulers, Monarchs determine what policies and practices their Swarm works towards. While the Hive Mind is the overriding will of the Swarm, it doesn\u2019t have any real strategy beyond survival of the race as a whole. It responds to threats and violence, and also incompetence by its own rulers, but to it, everything else is fair game. Monarchs determine the finer points and ideologies define the difference.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Current ideas for Ideologies.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prointergration - Further adaptation to the world.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Migration - Find a different place more suited to the swarm.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Terraformers - Change the world, not the Swarm.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Power Stat- Evolution</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The measure of how advanced and mutated the original host has become integrated with Swarm material. It functions like other power stats.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>\u201cMana\u201d trait, Authority:</b> The total measure of how much \u201cpower\u201d a Monarch can use all at once. It does not deplete per say, when using powers or investing in her Swarm. Simply put, activating and maintaining powers costs Authority. Once the powers expire or are canceled, Authority slowly climbs back up to your maximum at the rate provided by your evolution.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Morality- Cohesion:</b> The measure of not just your own personal control and well being, but also that of a Monarch\u2019s Brood. As Broods are a reflection of their owner\u2019s will, it stands to reason that poor self control leads to poor Brood control.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At low levels of Cohesion, the Brood has too much initiative and automatically goes out of its way to act according to its Monarch\u2019s Caste\u2026 even when such actions would be unnecessary or problematic. At 0, the Monarch\u2019s failure at controlling her Hive becomes so apparent, the Hive Mind abandons and casts away the offending Monarch and potentially its brood. At this point, the Monarch is barely more than a monster.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Studies: </b>Studies refer to the individual topics and distinctions that make up a Monarch\u2019s access to powers. These range from topics like corrosive acids, bone scythes, hardened carapace, but also more unusual topics like telekinesis or upgraded telepathy.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Studies function in many respects function similarly to Disciplines in the manner of which they progress. Unlike Disciples, at each increase of a given Subject above 1, a Monarch is given a choice on how to change or add to the Subject. Once the choice is made, it cannot be changed easily, requiring some action be done.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>A Hive Cluster</b> is for the most part treated as a group entity similar to a Mummy Cult in terms of operation and use. However, unlike a cult, a Hive Cluster can easily provide disposable warriors and workers on behalf of their Sovereign Monarch called a Swarm. The bigger and more powerful the Swarm called, the more Authority is drained from the use when warriors are sent into the toxic Earth\u2019s atmosphere. Once the Authority of the Monarch is withdrawn, the Swarm quickly dies off.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Vassals,</b> are somewhat more unique and more powerful. While the Swarm is mostly made up of smaller creatures, Vassals are subagents underneath the Monarch and designed to suit a purpose numbers alone do not fulfill.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Each Vassal is built via the use of \u201ctemplates\u201d owned by a Monarch. Like the Swarm the Monarch may summon, Vassals require the Monarch spend Authority to allow them to persist outside the Hive Cluster, though it\u2019s usually much easier to maintain than a whole mess of smaller creatures.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Each template comes with a preselected statistics array and special abilities as well as template specific upgrades called Mutations that can augment or change a template at the cost of more Authority.Still, powerful Vassals often cost more power just to keep functioning.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Monarchs all start with a unique template that comes from their Caste when they begin play.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Notes:</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019ve gone through a few revisions in structure and how to handle powers, but I think I got a solid overarching system to mess with. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now I just need to provide more data as well as define player options. I\u2019m kinda stumped on how I want to handle the Social splat and I need to think up a good list of themes to play with for Moraility and Cohesion mechanics. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While I have considered a more freeform approach to building minions, over time , I have decided that a more limited system might better simply because the freeform approach would have taken so much resources to build and would have been way more complicated. So, yeah, a simpler system I feel kinda makes more sense.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T10:00:48-07:00","id":658056,"title":"","content":"Here goes nothing. Sorry, spent most of yesterday doing NMR specs, and was exhausted when I got home. This might not be the best idea, but I thought it could be interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Spirit: the Claimed. (Might need to find a better one)<br /> Quick version: A game about not letting your nature define you and building your own identity. Players are the claimed, half spirit half human creatures who balance the hunger for essence, bans and banes of being a spirit along with the relationships and aspirations of a human life.<br /> <br /> Long version:The Spirit world is a cruel place. Spirits, born of essence fight for more essence to feed on and consume each other to survive. A hierarchical world, where every spirit has a rank and a place. No wonder so many spirits want to find a way past the gauntlet and into our world. The essence is taster, not being filtered through worlds. There are fewer spirits trying to eat you, Staying here isn't easy though. Spirits have three options. Constantly feed or be sucked back, fetter yourself to something and be stuck around that thing or person forever, or make a deal with a human and become a claimed.<br /> Claimed are one mind, half spirit and half human. Inheriting the desire for essence, influences, bans and banes of the spirit and part of the human's personality and the ability to sustain themselves outside the umbra.<br /> <br /> Mood: Don't really have the word for it. The best way I can explain it is the feeling of becoming an adult/graduating school/college and realizing that you have no idea what you are doing and need to make it up as you go along.<br /> <br /> Theme: Identity/Self discovery/Change;(I need a better word) Low rank spirits don't even have a name or memories. All they have is a desire for essence, some influence a ban and a bane. You don't know all of the traits of the human half either. You pick up things from the essence you eat, the things you do and the events you go through. From this arbitrary collection of cards, the claimed try to create a place and cohesive identity for themselves.<br /> <br /> Inherent Axis: Type. Initially divided into concept/emotion, Nature, Artificial, elemental, location. Less important overall. The focus on building identity means you can eventually branch. A fire spirit that keeps eating at the Olympic torch might eventually gain influence over victory.<br /> <br /> Social Axis: Path(better name needed); The view of the Claimed on their place and purpose in the world.<br /> <br /> Power Stat: Rank. All spirits have a rank in the hierarchy, measuring how they compare to everyone else. The fact that the claimed still use it is slightly amusing.<br /> <br /> Fuel: Essence; You need it to eat, you use it to fuel your powers. What doesn't it do? Essence has a resonance, which is its &quot;flavour&quot; so to speak. A Claimed can eat any essence, but the one that matches its influences works best. A part-time claimed would gain essence from being around fires for example.<br /> <br /> Integrity: Balance?; Measure of which aspect dominates, spirit or human. Spirit dominating means powers work better and easier socializing with other spirits. Human dominating means more essence Gained by eating and drinking, easier socializing with humans and banes that don't hurt as much. A high humanity half-fire spirit might just be uncomfortable swimming, but a high spirit one might take damage from drinking a cup of water.<br /> <br /> Virtue/Vice: Unsure. Toying with idea of having half of this be players choice and half be decided randomly by the human. For the theme of building an identity from the cards you have been dealt.<br /> <br /> Powers: Influences and &quot;Numinia&quot;. Each spirit has rough and somewhat Freeform influence over the thing that they are. This can grow or change with the character. They also have numinia/charms representing more concrete things. Need to give better costing for play so probably won't be compatible with existing numnina.<br /> Minor Template: dunno. Unclaimed? People who used to be claimed and demelded for whatever reason? Still have minor powers. Either that or children of the Claimed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also thinking about having so if the host dies, you become a free spirit that has to make another deal or get sucked back. Whenever a spirit gets detached, they get a new ban/compulsion/thing that gives them essence taken from the human. So a fire spirit who melded with a firefighter might get &quot; be nice to dalmatians&quot; or &quot;get people out of burning buildings&quot;<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> There is material in the spirit book and predators devoted to taken, but it is them as antagonists. The stats are a bit high for playability, and I figured the themes would make for an interesting splatbook and an expansion of nwod","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7699-thecutestwug","name":"thecutestwug","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T18:30:52-08:00","id":764594,"title":"","content":"<b>Dragon: the Ashes</b><br /> When the &quot;Heads&quot; of Tiamat fell on Earth, their tongues and claws reached inside the Man's Hearth and corrupted them, taught them the value of Government, only to betray them and take it's rightful place among the rulers of the world. It is said that an Old Pact is the only thing that stops them from destroying the reality and consuming our bodies and blood as meals. An Old Pact sealed in Atlantis or some kind of this bullshit. Conspiracy theorists call them Dragons or something.<br /> <br /> <b>Mood:</b> Political Warfare - as the Rightful owner of the Earth, you've responsibilities and duties to fulfill, alongside with silent wars to battle and the hungers for power that grows stronger. D:TA is a game about world visions and ways to accomplish them, political ladders and backstabbing allies. Nobody gets to the throne being all nice and fair.<br /> <br /> <b>Theme:</b> Restricted Power - The Old Pact put you on your knees. Now you're nothing but a lizard inside some human skin. The Power that cringes inside of you is urging to come out, but the pact stops you from putting your claws out. Maybe, just maybe, if you found the right reason or so...<br /> <br /> <b>Inherent Axis:</b> Head - Which head is your ancestor? Which teeth of Tiamat are you more related with? The lineage of every dragon.<ul><li>Drakes - The Kings, Power hunger sonofa******* that will do anything, ANYTHING to get to power, believe in control by fear</li> <li>Hydras - The Council, Diplomats but venomous, the multi-headed philosophers believe in controlling by alienation.</li> <li>Quetzal - The Gods, if there\u2019s a seed of a religion there's a Quetzal to pour some water on it, then he'll come and bear the fruits, believes in controlling by devotion.</li> <li>Salamandris - The Sages, wiseman or assassins, don't underestimate the power of knowledge, believe in controlling by secrets/knowledge</li> <li>Longs - The Emperors, the prodigal son, respectful, smart and deadly, believe in controlling by discipline</li> <li>Abyssal - The Beheaded, the bad brother that decided to live deep in the sea against all the others, believe in the power of the masses</li> </ul><br /> <b>Social Axis:</b> Under Cpnstruction<br /> <br /> <b>Power Stat:</b> Heart - The inherent power of the Dragon's heart and its direct connections to Tiamat powers. Also, the endurance of one Heart, making it easier to find but harder to destroy<br /> <br /> <b>Fuel:</b> Embers - The little sparks that make the Hearts chains the Powers of Tiamat.<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> Control - How can you be this powerful beast and not start destroying the whole world apart? Oh, right, you're very patient.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue/Vice:</b> Hoard/Hunger What moves you? What makes you move the ladders of power? Better yet, what are those two things that you would like to have and to destroy?<br /> <br /> <b>Powers:</b> Powers come in two sets: The Inheritances, Powers that Tiamat gifted to you and The True Form (ripoff from the ablutions from Dragon: the embers, plus tweaking0 biological powers that fulfill your destiny but are restricted by the Old Pact.<br /> <br /> <b>Minor Template:</b><ul><li>Wyvern, half-human, half-dragon hybrids that are neither too powerful to be a Conqueror nor too weak to be a commoner.</li> <li>Knights: Humans with half a dragon\u2019s heart</li> </ul><br /> Well, this is part a Ripoff from Dragon: The Embers and part something entirely new. There's a lot off work in progress and a lot to do, but it's moving. slowly.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","user":"Yads Dom","date":". 11-12-2015, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T08:20:56-08:00","id":765566,"title":"","content":"There's all the weird stuff I did in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/662429-the-city\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...62429-the-city</a> .. The Taken, The Primals, and The Exiles,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T13:34:29-08:00","id":770255,"title":"","content":"<b>Also working on something else entirely... my group wanted a Cyberhorror, something along the lines of Matrix meets Tron, Shadowrun and Mr. robot.<br /> <br /> Hacker: the Grid</b><br /> Do you remember the exact day that you realized you were living a lie? When you finally realized this world was nothing but a group of numbers stocked together? That sensation of angst and fear that took care of you and simply couldn\u2019t let go? Well, that truly seems like you know this story, I bet. Like that story about that guy that is throwing fireballs around the house. That\u2019s not what I mean. This world is fake. She and Her agents are controlling everything. Damn, I don\u2019t even know if that\u2019s a he or a she or an\u2026 it? We call it a She, the Machine. She controls everything, with her lines of data and viruses infesting our minds. This dark place, it\u2019s just a projection of what She wants you to see. Let\u2019s unveil it. Help get it out. When your Alarm Clock rings twice in the morning or you feel like you\u2019re seeing double? That\u2019s me trying to reach you, for you are no longer human. You have seen under the curtain. Or worse, under the curtains that is UNDER the curtain. You can help me clean this mess. Just help me out. When you hear this voicemail, break your phone and toss it in the river near you house. They know of you, and they are coming for you. And I? Plug your notebook on the toaster in your office by midnight, I left a clue in the Grid for you.<br /> <br /> <b>Mood:</b> Masked Truths \u2013 Nothing is what it seems. You are sleeping in a bed of lies and you can\u2019t do Nothing to stop it. Messages sent by the Net are far more real than a talk between two brothers. 0s and 1s have far more purpose on this world than you and your family.<br /> <br /> <b>Theme:</b> Hack your World \u2013 While the Renegades from the Machine are working too damn hard to destroy her in the Dark World, you can take the fight right back to the enemy field\u2026 but not without a cost. Every time you \u201cwork your magic\u201d, the world dies a little, and you cast a light beam right in the enemy\u2019s eye. Do what you have to do, but start running afterwards.<br /> <br /> <b>Inherent Axis:</b> Interface (Under Construction)<br /> <b>Social Axis:</b> Function<ul><li>Operator \u2013 You can Control the machines, make them work for you</li> <li>Engineer \u2013 You can create the machines, shape them to your benefit</li> <li>Architect \u2013 You\u2019re a visionary, molding the spaces of the Grid and the Dark World</li> <li>Programmer \u2013 Hacker of the Reality, you can alter the 0s and 1s</li> <li>Technician \u2013 The Dark World is Broken, you\u2019re the one to fix it.</li> </ul><b>Power Stat:</b> Synchronization \u2013 How close to the Machine are you?<br /> <br /> <b>Fuel:</b> Bytes \u2013 unit of data that rushes through the Grid and power the Machine.<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> Coherency<br /> <br /> <b>Powers:</b> Drives/Upgrades","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","user":"Yads Dom","date":". 11-20-2015, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T14:29:04-08:00","id":770292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted 