s and 1s have far more purpose on this world than you and your family.<br /> <br /> <b>Theme:</b> Hack your World \u2013 While the Renegades from the Machine are working too damn hard to destroy her in the Dark World, you can take the fight right back to the enemy field\u2026 but not without a cost. Every time you \u201cwork your magic\u201d, the world dies a little, and you cast a light beam right in the enemy\u2019s eye. Do what you have to do, but start running afterwards.<br /> <br /> <b>Inherent Axis:</b> Interface (Under Construction)<br /> <b>Social Axis:</b> Function<ul><li>Operator \u2013 You can Control the machines, make them work for you</li> <li>Engineer \u2013 You can create the machines, shape them to your benefit</li> <li>Architect \u2013 You\u2019re a visionary, molding the spaces of the Grid and the Dark World</li> <li>Programmer \u2013 Hacker of the Reality, you can alter the 0s and 1s</li> <li>Technician \u2013 The Dark World is Broken, you\u2019re the one to fix it.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Power Stat:</b> Synchronization \u2013 How close to the Machine are you?<br /> <br /> <b>Fuel:</b> Bytes \u2013 unit of data that rushes through the Grid and power the Machine.<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> ?<br /> <br /> <b>Powers:</b> Drives/Upgrades</div> </div> </div> </div>This feels like it could be done with a Mage Hack, honestly. I don't know if the concept as you've presented it is sufficient to stand on its own as a full splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T14:47:14-08:00","id":770303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=770255#post770255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Also working on something else entirely... my group wanted a Cyberhorror<br /> <br /> Hacker: the Grid</b></div> </div> </div> </div> So, like a Stigmatics+ gameline? Interesting idea. As for Integrity, maybe <b>Coherency</b>? Like, it measures how well you're able to handle the truth/stay under the radar, and as you go lower you find it harder to understand what's real and what's fake as you grow more and more of a blatant anomaly, finally ending in you becoming an insane and inhuman &quot;corrupted file&quot; at 0?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T17:36:37-08:00","id":770398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=770292#post770292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This feels like it could be done with a Mage Hack, honestly. I don't know if the concept as you've presented it is sufficient to stand on its own as a full splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>it could, actually, but me and my group hate some mechanics and some other aspects of Mage, so we decided that we wanted something that could work along the lines of Matrix meets Tron, Shadowrun and Mr. Robot. That said, we have lots to work on, yet.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, the ideia of Humans interacting with the God-Machine and going to a &quot;Supernal World&quot; called The Grid (Tron Reference and all) was toying in my head too much. \u200b<br /> <br /> Edit2: Also, I was sure that the Mage hack thing would come up, that's why there's a joke about it in the description hehehe<br /> <br /> Edit3: Also, Malonkey, fell in love with your Shaman Splat, if you're willing to continue work on it, i'm interested in helping\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","user":"Yads Dom","date":". 11-20-2015, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T17:37:38-08:00","id":770400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=770303#post770303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, like a Stigmatics+ gameline? Interesting idea. As for Integrity, maybe <b>Coherency</b>? Like, it measures how well you're able to handle the truth/stay under the radar, and as you go lower you find it harder to understand what's real and what's fake as you grow more and more of a blatant anomaly, finally ending in you becoming an insane and inhuman &quot;corrupted file&quot; at 0?</div> </div> </div> </div> I SO LOVED THIS!!!\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T21:10:08-08:00","id":772050,"title":"","content":"This thread reminded me of an idea I had. This idea was inspired abit by Bayonetta, Devil May Cry, the Inferno Supplement to the New World of Darkness and abit of negative feelings from the concept of the God Machine (I just didn't like the idea of a malfunctioning Divine Calculator and demons/angels becoming technospies/reality hackers). I'm sorry if what I said was bad and if I post the idea a<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">nyways. Long sections shall be put into spoilers to make the post overall shorter and to avoid &quot;TL;DR&quot;. Anyways, this is my first time here, I'm sorry if I post badly and it's nice to meet you all. :3</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Demon: The Infernal</b></span></span> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You were once a human. Walking around on earth, doing mundane things, basically living life as reality ordained. Sure, you did one or two bad things. But you\u2019re ultimately human. It\u2019s normal to kill several people or extort people over their lifetime, right? Or you did several bad things over the course of your life, but that\u2019s normal too. You could\u2019ve been an angel too if were good enough to rise to a higher state and you commanded the world to follow your leaders whims. </div></div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">But you\u2019re not either of those things. Not anymore. When you fucked up enough, you were cast down from the cosmos or you got dragged from your rotting corpse and into the stinking Inferno, where the worst of humanity lies and the power rule over the strong. Here, you were changed, tortured, beaten and twisted completely at the whims of the denziens there. And the worst thing is, Inferno is a nigh inescapable prison for people like you, and from when you entered YOU became a citizen of Inferno. In other words, you\u2019re a Demon. And your kind has existed since time immemorial as an example to what happens to evil folks and angels for what happens to good folks.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">But times change, and so do people and places. And because the concept of &quot;Good get rewarded, evil get punished&quot; is becoming borked, the Inferno is no longer an inescapable prison! Sure, a Demon or two has been called out because they left some part of their legend in the human world, but now they can leave without that restriction! You\u2019d think this was bad, but what would it mean if you wanted to leave and redeem yourself? A broken prison is still a prison, and many of the power mad are glad to wallow in the maggot pile. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Oh, and don\u2019t think that the Angels are the absolute good guys. Humanity as a whole is beginning to lose faith in the higher, and lower, powers, and as such they are suffering for it. From the gates of Paradiso, the Angels fly and follow the orders of their leaders to bring the world back into their clutches as it was long ago. Those who don\u2019t follow them to the letter tend to not do anything anymore. </span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Mood: Temptation (Might need changing or heavy revision)</b><br /> You're a big bad demon now, there's not much worse that you can do, is there? You've been tortured for Creator knows how long, so it's fine to use the same stuff onto other people, right? All Demons have this temptation, the stigma that comes with being &quot;the demon&quot; to just act it out. Not to mention that you were once human, and if you reject that and embrace the torment then you might as well have not escaped at all.<br /> <br /> <b>Theme: Liberation (Might also need changing, general idea is a mix of free will with personal responsibility)</b><br /> Free will has been a thing for humans, and even moreso for Demons who introduced it to the world. Most Demons seem to long for freedom. From the Inferno, from the rule of Paradiso, and some of the worse off ones from morality and constraint. <br /> <br /> <b>Inherent Axis: Houses - </b>Formed usually through how the once human committed the &quot;crimes&quot; that condemned them to Inferno and made part of them as a Demon.<br /> Consumer: The Devourers who go through people and all they know to gain their wants and needs.<br /> Controllers: The Defilers who wield themselves and their powers through force.<br /> Tempters: Fiends who know that knowledge is power and seek it at all costs.<br /> Twisters: The Malefactors who twist people and reality to their whims.<br /> Whisperers: The Devils who inspire cruelty and brother against brother.<br /> <br /> <b>Outside Axis: Circles </b>- How demons come together based on idealeology and how they deal with threats from Paradiso and keeping the worse demons sealed in Inferno.<br /> Limbo: The &quot;Humanity F*** Yeah&quot; faction. They tend to focus on human ingenuity and reason as a weapon against Angels.<br /> Heresy: The Community Faction. Seek to bring all of humanity together by destroying the imaginary boundaries that both humans and Angels have made to separate them.<br /> Violence: The Fighting Faction. Decided it's best to fight Hellfire with Hellfire, and they fight to destroy threats to Demons and throw the Hellbound back to Inferno.<br /> Fraud: The Knowledge Faction. They tend to hold onto demonic lore as well as acting as info brokers, spies and assassins, and even abit of witness protection for demons.<br /> Treachery: The Political Faction. They believe that the collective will and faith of humanity is powerful (it's what made Inferno into an impenetrable prison) and seek to wield it against their enemies.<br /> <br /> <b>Supernatural Advantage: Infernal Rank</b><br /> Inferno is a realm where power rules over all, and those with the most power rule the most. Infernal Rank is the measure of power a Demon holds, how many Pacts and Thralls he can maintain at one time as well as how much Faith the Demon can hold. However, the higher it is, the more her otherworldly and ultimately defiling power shows through her mortal form. Did I also mention that Demons can be pulled back to Inferno if they're hostless? Those with higher Infernal Rank face more danger of that actually happening.<br /> <br /> <b>Fuel Stat: Faith (Looking for a different name or something that isn't clearly so connected to Demon the Fallen)</b><br /> Faith is a powerful tool that only mortals are capable of creating, the trust in someone or something. It is the power of the Celestials and what gives them power....because humanity gives them that power. Because of human faith, they believe that natural disasters are divine punishment or curses and attribute them to gods and demons alike. It was the trust that &quot;Evil is punished and good is rewarded&quot; is the reason that Inferno is an impenetrable prison and Paradiso remains a paradise despite it's corrupt nature.<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity: Grace (Need help on clarifying or what it should be like)</b><br /> Grace isn't beauty or tasteful clothing, it's a state of mind of how one is and how they are. To Demons, this means their sense of self-identity after the harrowing torments of Inferno labelling them as just &quot;a criminal&quot;. High Grace makes it easier for Demons to remain in the Human World and interact, and even feel less of a tug from Inferno while hostless. Those with low Grace stick out like a sore thumb as beings who are steadily becoming like their tormentors. Grace 0 Demons are known as &quot;Hellbound&quot;, those who seek to bring the Inferno to earth and make the world into a new Inferno.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue/Vice: </b>Basically the same as a regular humans.<br /> <br /> <b>Powers: </b><b>Dominions. </b>If Faith is what gives Demons the ability to move mountains, then it's Dominions that give them the actual oomph to do so. Dominions are what Angels lay their claim on reality over, and it's what Demons kept. <br /> <br /> <b>Minor Templates: </b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Nothing can ever get close to the corruption of Demonhood without becoming fully corrupted themselves. These two templates are human in every way, save that they have the backing of a supernaturally powerful spirit or aid it somehow.<br /> <b>Thralls: </b>People who serve the Demon and/or have the backing of. At the least, a thrall is someone who maintains a pact with the Demon, in which the person gains a benefit from the demon while the Demon gains Faith in return for upholding his end.<br /> <b>Masters: </b>Based abit off of Black Butler, the Masters are long term contractors of a Demon. Often, a Master has a sigil of the demon somewhere on his body and the demon must do anything the contractor says (and it cannot violate the pact created, so no self-destructive orders (which includes killing the master as much as it includes making the demon &quot;kill&quot; itself)) and in return when the time the servitude is completed or when the task the Master wants is done, the Demon recieves an extensive benefit (usually nomming up the Master's soul and claiming his body to possess).<br /> <b>Hosts: </b>Technically NOT a minor template. Hosts are empty bodies or souls that a Demon MUST possess if they want to stay in the Human World and not be tugged back to Inferno. The Demon can learn some of the hosts most significant memories, but it takes time to learn them all. Until then, some people intimate to the person might be able to catch something being off. Demons with Masters are capable of forming a body of their own without need of a Host.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Antagonists</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Angels. </b>Yes, the goody two shoes guys are the antagonists. Long ago in the dawn of creation ,the Creator and his Angels ruled humanity from the city of Paradiso. However, some Angels were not content with some of the human lack of will, which some saw as slavery. In their attempt to free humanity from this, Humanity realized it's own potential and had once overthrew Paradiso with the help of the Angels that did spark free will. Those still loyal to Paradiso took grave offense, and with the Creator gone after the attack, their enraged counterattack lead to them showing humanity what happens to those who defy Paradiso and the will of the Creator (whom they could TOTALLY be getting wrong). From this, Inferno was born and upkept by Faith, and the Angels believe that if they subjugate humanity underneath Paradiso, slay and send all Demons back to Inferno and ultimately perhaps even destroy Free Will, then the Creator would come back. <br /> <br /> They represent unchanging principle and order to the point of tyranny. They try to control the masses through religion (of all kinds to avoid it being singularly abrahmic) to inspire blind faith and bring them underneath Paradiso's banner. Given that today's people are less religious overall than in the past, this is why Faith is dwindling and why &quot;Inferno isn't a prison anymore&quot; as well as some parts of Paradiso falling apart is why they're perhaps more desperate and active as ever. <br /> <br /> If there's any reason for people to believe there being any difference between Angels and Demons, at the best, the differences are just superficial. Take away everything that makes an angel an &quot;angel&quot; and a demon a &quot;demon&quot; and they'd be seen as the same thing. As such, Angels and Demons both share and wield alot of the same traits listed above, although with a few different names on both ends. Celestial Rank instead of Infernal Rank. Servants, Beneficiaries and Honorables instead of Thralls, Masters and Hosts. I haven't worked out any factions the Angels have.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T08:12:41-08:00","id":781145,"title":"","content":"I sorta have something like this. It started as a change of fluff to Geist: The Sin-Eaters, but as I kept working on it, it honestly became its own game line, albeit one that borrows 90% of its mechanics from another line. The fluff is so different, however, that I feel it's worth mentioning it here.<br /> <br /> I have an entire gdoc on it, and the thing is mostly completed (I'm just missing finishing up some homebrewed Keys I came up with). So let me just copypaste the important bits. I'm skipping the Morality system (Anamnesis) because it's based on 1e rules.<br /> <div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:22px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><u>Geist: The Defiance</u></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A game of wilful intervention and second chances.</span></i></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><u>Introduction</u></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201cI got him out, Jaye. I got him out. Same fire, every New Year\u2019s Eve, always targets lone old men. Same one that took me. But this time, I changed the ending. I killed the bastard dead and the old man got to live.\u201d</span></i></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The players play as geists, also known as the Bound. A geist is a special type of ghost that has the ability to possess its former body at will and give it a semblance of life. When a geist is in her body, it\u2019s said she\u2019s in Revenant form. When she\u2019s outside it, she\u2019s said to be in Wraith form.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Geists are created when a person dies with a terribly important unfinished business (as normal ghosts), but their death had some sort of supernatural component or involvement, even indirectly. Having some sort of supernatural talent also counts (fully supernatural creatures like vampires, mages, werewolves and the like do not usually return as geists, as their souls are generally too damaged or \u2018contaminated\u2019 by otherworldly powers, but there is a specific Ceremony that breaks this rule).</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">When three or more geists swear allegiance to each other through a special Ceremony, they are said to have formed a Pact.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><u>The Defiance</u></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Defiance is a philosophy that most (but not all) geists share. Defiants believe that free will is paramount, and that an act of will can break the tyranny of fate, just as they themselves defied the ultimate equaliser. Defiants take a far more active (and meddlesome) role in their turf than other geists. Believing themselves to be warriors against the predetermined, they often seek to save lives and meddle in the affairs of the supernatural around them. Defiants can prove to be the thorn on the side of a vampire that thinks she has a stranglehold of a neighbourhood, or a werewolf pack terrorising a stretch of the countryside.</div></div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Some Defiants seek to defy death at every turn, using special Ceremonies to foresee soon-to-occur deaths and prevent them. Many Defiants believe that in so doing, they are saving \u2018innocents\u2019 and striking back at whatever they hate. Others do so for the thrill of power.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Particularly meddlesome Defiants will swiftly make enemies of creatures more powerful than themselves, such as mages that can destroy them with a thought, werewolves with spirits by their side, centuries-old vampires, frightening fae creatures, mortals trained in the art of taking down the supernatural and more. Geists in general can put up a fight, particularly when a Pact displays the necessary teamwork to coordinate their manifestations to full effect, but that\u2019s not their true strength. What sets the Bound apart from all other creatures of the night is their stubborn refusal to die. A geist that seeks to take out a more powerful foe can do so through relentlessness, returning from the dead over and over until she finally grinds her adversary down. Defiants thrive in this fact, and many die with a laugh on their lips as they seek to unnerve and demoralise their opponents before their inevitable return.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The philosophy of Defiance is an old one, dating back to the Renaissance or perhaps even further back, to the Dark Ages. Given that geists do not age or die of natural causes, they find it relatively easy to pass on traditions and philosophies from one generation to the next. Entire Pacts have been formed by Defiants to join forces against a common foe, and such an act is colloquially referred to by the Bound community as \u2018taking a stance\u2019.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Counter-culture is always quick to spring up, and the philosophy that opposes Defiance also dates back at least a few centuries ago. The philosophy of Obedience is far rarer than its mainstream counterpart, but its adherents are still a prevalent minority in Bound society. Obedients hold that since every geist had a supernatural component in her death, and since that is by definition unnatural, then those deaths were never supposed to happen in the first place. Obedients believe that this defiance of death was, in fact, in accordance to fate (or the will of God/Allah/other divine beings) and therefore geists are the agents of fate\u2019s will. Obedients will alternatively work with or oppose Defiants, depending on their goals. Most Obedients will join forces with Defiants to take out anything unnatural, but will also oppose them if they seek to tamper with what they perceive to be the \u2018natural order of things\u2019.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Both Defiants and Obedients may join forces with mortals or other supernatural creatures if it aligns with their philosophical goals. For example, Obedients may join forces with Hunters to take out an ancient evil, while Defiants may join forces with Changelings to foil the plans of the True Fae.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Geists that adhere to no philosophy are uncommon but not unheard of, are more concerned with their own individual Purpose than any greater philosophical matter, and many hold both Obedients and Defiants in contempt for their own personal reasons.</span></span></span></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><u>Purpose</u></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">All geists have a Purpose. This is the reason they refused passage towards the afterlife, and instead willed themselves to remain on Earth, defying death itself. Each Bound has her own individual Purpose, and fulfilling it becomes her mission in (un)life.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div></div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A geist that fulfills her Purpose has two options: they can dissolve their tether to their Anchor(s) and \u201cpass on\u201d to the afterlife, or they can attain a new Purpose. Even if one of the Bound is willing to pass on, it still requires an act of will to dissolve her connection to her Anchor. She must roll Resolve + Anamnesis as an extended action (rolling once per hour) and obtain as many total successes as her Psyche. She is allowed to spend Willpower on these rolls, but she may not augment her dice pool in any other way.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If a geist has more than one Anchor, she must do this extended roll for each and every one of her Anchors. Willingly dissolving her connection to her Anchor does not cause the Bound to take Aggravated damage (see Anchors section). However, when she finishes dissolving her connection to the last of her Anchors, she passes on to the afterlife. Once the geist begins the process of dissolving her ties to her Anchors, she cannot stop. </span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">When she passes on, her body drops dead on the spot, and the passage of time from the moment she originally died to the present accrue in a matter of seconds, aging the corpse correspondingly.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Attaining a new Purpose is a reflexive action that requires a successful roll with her Anamnesis dots as her dice pool. This dice pool may not be augmented in any way and may only be attempted once per day. </span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A geist that resolves her Purpose need not choose immediately. She may elect to take a few days to \u201cleave her affairs in order\u201d before choosing to dissolve her connections to her Anchors, or consult with sources of guidance before resolving to attain a new Purpose. However, every day that a geist goes by without a Purpose, she takes one point of Aggravated damage at dawn and is unable to hold Plasm within her body. This damage may not be healed until the geist attains a new Purpose.</span></span></span></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><u>Anchor</u></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Bound begin play with one Anchor. An Anchor can take the form of a place, object or person, and binds the geist to the world of the living. A geist is not damaged if her Anchor is, until the Anchor is completely destroyed. Every day that one of the Bound goes without an Anchor, she takes one point of Aggravated damage at dawn. This damage cannot be healed by any means and is cumulative, which gives geists anywhere from 5 days to two weeks (depending on their Health) to bind themselves to a new Anchor.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div></div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The process of binding to an Anchor is a Ceremony that every geist begins knowing for free (see Anchor the Soul). Performing the Ceremony varies for every geist. It\u2019s a unique process that reflects some aspect of the geist\u2019s personality and/or past.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">As the Bound gains Psyche, she increases the amount of Anchors she needs. Every Anchor that is destroyed inflicts the point of Aggravated damage per day, so having multiple Anchors destroyed at once can be particularly devastating for a high-Psyche geist.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A geist must remain within 10 miles per dot of Psyche from all their Anchors. Failure to do so inflicts 1 point of Aggravated damage at dawn for each day she remains too far from her Anchor.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A geist with multiple Anchors may move between two of them while in Wraith form by spending a point of Willpower. She must be within 1 yard per point of Psyche of one of her Anchors in order to do so. She must still respect her Wraith form limitations.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Geists may not bind themselves to new Anchors if they are already at their maximum for their Psyche. If they gain Psyche and it requires them to bind with a new Anchor, they must perform the Anchor the Soul Ceremony before the sun next rises or they begin to take Aggravated damage.</span></span></span></div></div></div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><br /> <br /> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><u>Geist Physiology</u></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Geists have a +4 bonus to any rolls related to entering places of death (graveyards, mausoleums, morgues, murder scenes, places of recent/frequent death, etc.). This bonus applies to rolls of diverse nature, from picking a lock to breaking down a door to pushing through a defensive ward. Geists belong in places of death, and keeping one out of them is a difficult task indeed.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Revenant Form</span></i></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lifelike Appearance</span></i></span></span><br /> <div align=\"left\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">While in their Revenant form, geists are undead beings that can easily pretend to be alive. So long as the Bound has at least 1 point of Plasm in reserve, she looks alive and fools anything short of supernatural scrutiny. Even in this lifelike state, geists do not age or die of natural causes.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div></div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">She can still be poisoned, drugged, irradiated or fall ill, but she gains a +2 to all rolls to overcome those afflictions (the Stricken gain a +5 instead). She can still starve or die of thirst, but she gains a +2 to all rolls to overcome those afflictions (the Silent gain a +5 instead). She can still suffer exposure or the ill effects of weather and temperature variations, but she gains a +2 to all rolls to overcome those afflictions (the Prey gain a +5 instead). She can still suffer the damage of accidental physical impact (such as falling, explosives or objects crashing against her), but she gains a +2 to all rolls to resist or evade them (the Forgotten gain a +5 instead). She can still be deliberately harmed, but the Torn do not suffer wound penalties.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Geists with Plasm in their reserves may spend it to ablate wounds as explained in the core book rules.</span></span></span></div></div></div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">True Mien</span></i></span></span><br /> <div align=\"left\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">When a geist runs out of Plasm in her Revenant form, she loses her lifelike appearance, revealing her true mien. She looks clearly undead, cold and lacking any vital signs, bearing the wounds or signs of whatever killed her (though the Phantasmal Key can disguise this). When this happens, however, she gains beneficial undead traits that increase her durability. She does not take wound penalties and is immune to suffocation, thirst, starvation, illness, radiation, pressure, vacuum, exposure, temperature variations (as long as they stay outside extreme temperatures), unconsciousness, and any form of mundane drugs or poison. She also takes Bashing damage from all weaponry (including firearms) and from physical impacts (such as falling, objects crashing against her, explosives, etc.). Extreme heat (including fire) and extreme cold deal Lethal damage as normal, as does any superheated or supercooled material.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div></div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A geist with no Plasm in their reservoir may reflexively spend a point of Willpower to retain or regain their lifelike appearance for a scene. Doing this does not grant them the resilience of their undead form but allows them to hide their true mien in a pinch. Once this expenditure has been made, the Bound cannot lose the lifelike appearance until the scene ends.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If one of the Bound was afflicted with a condition that they would be immune to if they ran out of Plasm (such as an illness or drug), it is cleansed from their bodies when they do so. If they later acquired Plasm or spent Willpower to regain their lifelike appearance, that condition would be gone.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Whether by an ancient oath or by the very nature of their power, a Bound\u2019s role in the world is to act unseen, save against those that matter to them personally. Geists that allow mortals to witness their true mien receive a -5 to all dice pools when attempting to affect that mortal with Manifestations or other supernatural effects. However, if the mortal is someone that is part of their Purpose (such as \u201cthe man that killed me\u201d or \u201cthe child I swore to protect\u201d), that penalty becomes a +3 bonus instead. This penalty/bonus lasts forever, unless someone finds a way to make the mortal forget what they saw. Being seen in their true mien by more than one person imposes a -1 to all rolls to unlock Manifestations, perform Ceremonies or do anything supernatural. This stacks per additional person, up to a -5. This penalty also stacks with the previous bonus/penalty, if applicable, and lasts for as long as the mortals are observing the geist\u2019s true mien.</span></span></span></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Wraith Form</span></i></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Geists in their Wraith form do not exist in the material plane, but in Twilight, like ordinary ghosts. In that form, they are immune to all forms of damage, save for supernatural attacks that deal Aggravated damage (and only from attackers who can affect them in Twilight). However, Bound in Wraith form may manifest briefly if unlocking a Manifestation (or altering/ending its effects) requires them to make temporary physical contact with the world. Some ceremonies may (or must) be performed in Wraith form. If they require making physical contact with the world, the geist manifests briefly to do so.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div></div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">There is a Ceremony that allows a geist in Wraith form to manifest like a ghost.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Geists in their Wraith form use their Psyche as extra Health. This takes the form of a visual effect around the Bound that fades as they take damage (some examples include an armour of shining steel, a sphere of fire, a swirl of rose petals or snowflakes, a ring of spinning blades, etc.). This extra Health lasts for as long as the Bound remains in Wraith form and, when spent to absorb damage, refreshes after a good night\u2019s sleep.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A geist in Wraith form cannot move further than 5 yards per point of Psyche from their corpse (though there is a Ceremony that affects this).</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A geist can only spend up to 1 hour per point of Psyche in Wraith form (though there is a Ceremony that affects this). Once her time\u2019s up, she\u2019s shunted back into her body.</span></span></span></div></div></div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Switching Forms</span></i></span></span><br /> <div align=\"left\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A geist may switch between Revenant and Wraith forms as an instant action. When one of the Bound shifts into Wraith form, her body goes unconscious. If her Plasm reserve is empty and she has not spent Willpower to make herself look lifelike, instead of going unconscious, the body simply collapses on the spot, looking like a fresh cadaver to any onlookers. A geist in Wraith form always looks freshly killed to any who can see into Twilight and is considered to be in her true mien automatically (though the Phantasmal Key can disguise this).</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div></div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Damage dealt to a geist\u2019s body while she\u2019s in Wraith form does not affect her until she returns to Revenant form. When she does, the damage that the body suffered is added to any Aggravated damage she may have taken while in Wraith form.</span></span></span></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Death Weakness</span></i></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">All of the Bound have a specific source of Aggravated damage that is unique to each of them. The specific nature of their death is their weakness. If an enemy can emulate the way the geist died (attacking her with the same type of weapon that killed her, for example), they are able to inflict Aggravated damage with it. Geists that died in a non-weaponizable way (exposure, illness, starvation, accident) instead allow enemies to roll Manipulation + either Persuasion or Expression - the geist\u2019s Composure as an instant action in order to revive the Bound\u2019s moment of death with their words and deal Aggravated damage.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div></div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">This specific weakness deals Aggravated damage whether it\u2019s inflicted to the geist on her Revenant or Wraith forms (if the enemy can see into Twilight, she may use a mundane weapon that does not affect ghosts, such as a common revolver, in order to deal Aggravated damage to one of the Bound in Wraith form, provided that weapon is the same type that killed her), but a geist can only be affected by her Death Weakness once per turn at most.</span></span></span></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Resonance Weakness</span></i></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Geists are vulnerable to blessed weaponry, just like ghosts are, but they are also vulnerable to particularly heinous, cursed artefacts. However, the Shroud manifestation protects them from such attacks, even if the blessing or curse says that it bypasses supernatural protections. The Shroud also protects against enchanted or ensorcelled weapons, even those designed to bypass supernatural defences. Only weapons crafted with death resonances designed to pierce the Shroud can ignore a Shroud\u2019s protection.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><u>Death</u></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Geists do not die as easily as other creatures, and instead defy death as a second nature. When one of the Bound would die but remains tied to at least one Anchor, she is instead revived at the following dawn with a caul over her face, and an innocent has died in her place (as explained in the corebook, the innocent dies in a manner that falls within the geist\u2019s Threshold, and the first thing that the Bound sees when she returns to life is the last few moments of that person\u2019s life). This event is an sin against Anamnesis 6. The geist returns in Revenant form regardless of what form she was in when she died. If the body was completely destroyed, she reappears in the place where she originally died the very first time.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div></div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If she was killed in the same way that she originally died, she suffers a major derangement (chosen between the Storyteller and the player) for one day per dot of Anamnesis below 7 (if the Bound has Anamnesis 7 or higher, the derangement still lasts for one day).</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If a geist is killed after having her Anchors destroyed (but she did not willingly choose to dissolve her connection to them), she does not return to life, and does not pass into the afterlife either. This event is referred to as vanquishing. A vanquished Bound becomes a faint echo in Twilight trapped in the area surrounding her, only audible by ghosts and other geists in Wraith form, and the Bound can only do so after succeeding a Wits + Psyche roll (attemptable only once per hour). If a Bound can hear this echo, she can only just barely communicate with the vanquished geist, though she must repeat her Wits + Psyche every so often (Storyteller\u2019s discretion) to ensure she can properly hear what the echo wishes to tell her.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A vanquished geist cannot use any of her powers, and influencing the world around her is nigh-impossible. She may attempt an extended roll of Presence + Psyche, Intelligence + Psyche or Strength + Psyche (whichever dice pool is highest) once per day (rolling once every hour) in order to cause slight supernatural manifestations in her surroundings (which depend on her personality and her current location). It takes at least 5 successes per day for a normal mortal to begin to suspect that their surroundings might be haunted. A mortal aware of the supernatural requires only 3 successes per day, and a fully supernatural creature requires only 1 success per day.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If her surroundings are deserted, a vanquished geist may draw nearby people to her with an extended roll of Manipulation + Psyche, Dexterity + Psyche or Wits + Psyche (whichever dice pool is highest) once per day. She requires 1 success per mile away from her location to the nearest person. People that feel drawn to the area do not immediately drop what they\u2019re doing and go; they may ignore the calling for several days, and the vanquished geist can only apply more pressure to the calling if she exceeds the previous day\u2019s successes. If the vanquished geist exceeds the number of successes she needs by 5 or more, the calling becomes irresistible, and the person in question usually travels to the location within the next day. People summoned this way often stay around for a couple of days, which gives a vanquished geist a chance to alert them of her presence. This calling prioritises ordinary mortals over supernatural creatures.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Once a person is aware of the vanquished geist\u2019s presence, the Bound may roll Manipulation + Psyche in order to influence the person towards a certain course of action. This action needs to be simple and direct, such as \u2018conduct a seance in this location\u2019 or \u2018get Rhea Wyatt to this place\u2019. Vanquished geists are able to communicate with ghosts clearly, which gives them a potential ally.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If a geist at Anamnesis 0 is vanquished, she does not leave an echo behind. To do so, she requires a sense of self, which the Wretched have lost completely. Vanquished Wretched are lost to oblivion, and most geists fear this fate more than anything else.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The same Ceremony that can make a geist out of a fully supernatural creature also allows echoes of vanquished geists to return (see Ceremonies below). A vanquished geist that is returned to unlife via this ceremony begins at Psyche 1 and their previous Anamnesis or Anamnesis 5, whichever is lower.</span></span></span></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><u>Psyche and Plasm</u></span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">New Psyche Table:</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #4bacc6\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Psyche</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #4bacc6\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Attribute Limit</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #4bacc6\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Max Plasm/Plasm Per Turn</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #4bacc6\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Anchors</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #4bacc6\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Shades</span></span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #d2eaf1\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">1</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #d2eaf1\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">5</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #d2eaf1\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">14/1</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #d2eaf1\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">1</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #d2eaf1\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">0</span></span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffffff\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">2</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffffff\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">5</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffffff\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">18/2</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffffff\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-fami