style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">6</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffffff\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">6</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffffff\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">40/7</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffffff\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">2</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffffff\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">3</span></span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #d2eaf1\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">7</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #d2eaf1\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">7</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #d2eaf1\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">50/10</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #d2eaf1\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">2</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #d2eaf1\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">4</span></span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffffff\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">8</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffffff\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">8</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffffff\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">60/15</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffffff\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">3</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffffff\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">4</span></span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #d2eaf1\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">9</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #d2eaf1\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">9</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #d2eaf1\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">75/20</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #d2eaf1\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">3</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #d2eaf1\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">5</span></span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffffff\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">10</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffffff\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">10</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffffff\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">100/25</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffffff\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">4</span></span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffffff\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">5</span></span></span></div></td> </tr> </table></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Shades are memories given a necrotic semblance of life. As a geist grows in power, so do their memories. A shade is an echo of a person important to the geist, that haunts them in their dreams and whenever they take Wraith form. Shades are not accurate in the slightest: they are distorted by the geist\u2019s feelings towards that person, and by the deleterious effects of memory. Shades are uncontrollable, but they\u2019re not actual people. Being slivers of the geist\u2019s subconscious, they do not have minds or souls of their own and are therefore immune to any effects, supernatural or otherwise, that can affect people, spirits or creatures. Given that they do not exist in the material world either, ways of affecting shades are extremely rare.</div></div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A shade is a distracting force (though not necessarily malicious; whether the shade harangues and demeans the geist or simply distracts her through other means is completely up to the player) and imposes a -1 penalty to any and all tasks in Wraith form. This penalty stacks per shade, so a Bound with Psyche 10 takes a -5 penalty to everything he does in Wraith form. There is a specific Ceremony that brings temporary appeasement to shades and allows the geist to avoid the penalty. Most of the time, shades are only visible to their own geist, but certain forms of supernatural scrutiny may reveal them to onlookers (Storyteller\u2019s discretion). Thankfully, shades give their Bound a reprieve while she\u2019s in Revenant form.</span></span></span></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Gaining Plasm</span></i></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">A geist may obtain Plasm in five ways:</div></div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">1) From Haunts, as described in the rulebook.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">2) Once per week, one of the Bound may regain anywhere from 1 to 10 Plasm (Storyteller\u2019s discretion) from making progress towards her Purpose. Significant acts of Defiance or Obedience may also count instead, if the geist follows these philosophies.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">3) When a ghost or geist relinquishes their ties to their Anchors and passes on to the afterlife, they release a surge of Plasm that invigorates all nearby Bound. This completely fills a Bound\u2019s Plasm reserves.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">4) Once per day, saving the life of an ordinary mortal (unaware of the supernatural) that would have died in the same manner as the geist\u2019s Threshold, at a significant risk for the Bound, may refill a percentage of the geist\u2019s Plasm reserves, from 10% to 100% (Storyteller\u2019s discretion, should be proportional to effort involved). This does not trigger if the geist\u2019s actions save lives indirectly. The Bound only gains this bonus if she directly intervenes at the moment of impending doom and saves that life through a significant effort.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">5) Each conclave has a specific form of regaining plasm (see Factions below).</span></span></span></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><u>Factions</u></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Given that geists can be around for a long time if they find reasons to keep on (un)living, they have established over the centuries an eclectic form of society throughout the world. Factions within the Bound community are called conclaves, from their ancient custom of holding meetings behind locked doors.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Gravestone Conclave</span></i></span></span><br /> <div align=\"left\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The oldest conclave still in existence, supposedly dating back to times before the Dark Ages, the Gravestone Conclave remains a pillar of geist society and the neutral faction to which others defer judgement to. Members of the Gravestone Conclave are called magistrates (though less-friendly appellations also exist), and they are instructed in the arts of diplomacy, patience and equanimity. Moderate to a fault, they are often criticised for being too slow to act, for apparent cowardice, and for not upholding the purpose of geists as agents of action. However, magistrates are quick to point out that they have acted at the times it counted and that they have remained a hale faction through the centuries for a reason. </span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div></div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Their power in Bound society derives mostly from their financial and political wealth, rather than through numbers or combat prowess, though they are renown for their mastery over locations. Magistrates are usually aware of their surroundings and adept at channeling their powers far and wide. It is practically unheard of for a magistrate to lack a Haunt, for example. Magistrates tend to keep an eye on and control (or own) graveyards and other places of death. Given their financial prowess, ownership of land comes second nature to them.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The conclave\u2019s structure is hierarchical and bureaucratic, with each city or region having a High Magistrate in charge, reporting to a national Gray Magistrate, who in turn reports to one of the twelve Supreme Magistrates that form the Gravestone Council. The Gravestone Council arranges yearly meetings to debate the latest news and chart the future course of the conclave, which they then pass on to the Gray Magistrates for implementation.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Admittance into the Gravestone Council involves a formal hearing with the local High Magistrate, who elaborates a report on the candidate and elevates it to the Gray Magistrate she answers to. If the Gray Magistrate agrees with the High Magistrate\u2019s conclusion to admit the candidate in, she sends back her approval and the High Magistrate in question arranges a formal ceremony to welcome the new magistrate into the conclave. All promotions are decided exclusively by the Gravestone Council, though they take reports from other magistrates into account.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Magistrates regain 1 to 5 Plasm when they align their virtue or vice to the conclave\u2019s teachings in some significant way (for example, a Temperate magistrate negotiating a truce between two Pacts ready to tear each other apart, or a Prideful magistrate successfully arbitrates a difficult decision after claiming she was the only one capable of finding the right answer).</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Magistrates have a +1 bonus on Politics, Investigation, Persuasion and Academics.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Magistrates may purchase dots in the Boneyard manifestation for New Dots x 5 rather than New Dots x 6.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Crossovers:</u></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Supernatural creatures affiliated with this conclave include vampires and mages.</span></span></span></div></div></div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Conclave of Aether</span></i></span></span><br /> <div align=\"left\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A somewhat old conclave arisen in Victorian times, the Conclave of Aether gathers the thinking minds of Bound society. More like a loosely affiliated club than a true power, the Conclave of Aether is more concerned with answering the age-old questions about death and discovering new forms of geist power than resolving mundane matters. Emulating scientific society, it has no hierarchy or leadership, and instead maintains libraries, laboratories and vaults around the world, as well as the Ethereal Network, a form of communication among members (which currently takes the form of an encrypted internet forum), where they share their findings away from prying eyes. Their power in Bound society derives mostly from their arcane lore, rare supernatural artefacts and information network. There\u2019s little that this Conclave does not know.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div></div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Members of the Conclave of Aether call themselves seekers and generally have periodic local gatherings in order to exchange useful information. Not all seekers are aloof and focused only on experimentation and abstract theories. Many seekers are active investigators, riddled with curiosity about their surroundings. The conclave as a whole has no agenda, and seekers are instead allowed to pursue their interests as they see fit. Admittance is decided by majority among the local seekers in an area. Though custom dictates the candidate present the conclave with some finding of interest, this is not strictly observed any longer. So long as her fellow seekers find her a worthy addition, a geist finds little impediment in gaining membership on this conclave. As such, there is no formal ceremony to welcome new seekers into the fold.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Seekers regain 1 to 5 Plasm when they align their virtue or vice with the pursuit of truth in some significant way (for example, a Charitable seeker discovering a new use for her manifestation that allows her to aid the underprivileged in her neighbourhood, or an Envious seeker finding extremely important dirt on her enemy).</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Seekers have a +1 bonus in all Occult, Computer, Medicine and Science rolls.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Seekers may purchase dots in the Oracle manifestation for New Dots x 5 rather than New Dots x 6.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Crossovers:</u></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Supernatural creatures affiliated with this conclave include changelings and mages.</span></span></span></div></div></div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Sanguine Conclave</span></i></span></span><br /> <div align=\"left\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The origins of the Sanguine Conclave are a matter of great debate in the Bound community. It\u2019s not a new conclave by any means, but no one can truly confirm how old it is. The Sanguine Conclave exerts a strong influence in geist society, wielding a considerable amount of power. Its members call themselves reapers and see themselves as the armed forces of the Bound community. The history of the Sanguine Conclave is filled with attempts to establish hierarchies and ranks and to later standarise these ranks, as each country had its own take on them.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div></div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Currently, reapers function as independent soldiers within a Pact, which report to a superior, or as Pacts of mostly reapers under the command of the most senior geist. The Sanguine Conclave has no ultimate authority outside a country. Each country has a hierarchy of reapers based on seniority, with the oldest reaper at the head. The ranks vary greatly from country to country, and even within states or provinces. One state may boast a proud military tradition and adopt the military rank, while another may adopt the ranks of the air force or the navy. Some areas have a blend of ranks from different parts of the armed forces, which causes reapers in other locations no end of frustration. Some entrepreneurial reapers have instead decided to fabricate a new hierarchy entirely, with the ambitious goal of standarising it globally.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Admittance into the Sanguine Conclave is quite easy, and most reapers are out there recruiting. Reapers tend to be a tightly knit conclave where loyalty is paramount; and a reaper is always glad to train a new member in diverse forms of combat or help them develop their powers. Welcoming ceremonies vary from place to place. Reapers, unlike most other conclaves, remain in touch quite often, and they have a strong sense of tit for tat when it comes to reinforcements. A reaper may count with the aid of her brothers in arms, but she will be expected to drop whatever she\u2019s doing the moment a fellow reaper needs her aid.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Reapers regain 1 to 5 Plasm whenever their vice or virtue shines through in a difficult battle (for example, a Just reaper taking on a gang that has been terrorising her neighbourhood, or a Wrathful reaper letting her temper get the best of her and starting a fight with a powerful werewolf).</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Reapers have a +1 bonus in all Firearms, Weaponry, Brawl and Athletics rolls.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Reapers may purchase dots in the Rage manifestation for New Dots x 5 rather than New Dots x 6.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Crossovers:</u></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Supernatural creatures affiliated with this conclave include werewolves and hunters.</span></span></span></div></div></div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Conclave of the Unbroken Shield</span></i></span></span><br /> <div align=\"left\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Dating back to the late Renaissance, the Conclave of the Unbroken Shield is a group that prefers to remain invisible until it is time to intervene. Its members call themselves wardens and have taken upon themselves the task of seeking out and exterminating large-scale threats to humanity. The conclave does not have a hierarchy, as it considers all members equal. Wardens are allowed to do as they please with their time, so long as they keep a watchful eye. When a member of the conclave spots something grave, it contacts all nearby wardens in the surrounding areas, and they organise a reconnaissance together. If a majority of the wardens agree that the threat qualifies as large-scale, they allow each warden to marshall whatever allies they believe they can trust (and they are expected to answer for their allies\u2019 actions), and then they organise a swift and decisive strike.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div></div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The shape of the threat may be anything from an ancient vampire to a mass-murdering werewolf to an abyssal horror to things so antithetical to life that they have no name. Wardens are generally a serious bunch, who value efficiency, patience and decisive action. Admittance to the conclave is not easy, as wardens are secretive and slow to trust. Candidates require a warden to vouch for them, and then they must earn the approval of at least the majority of the wardens in the region (what exactly constitutes as a region varies from country to country). They have no welcoming ceremony. Wardens rarely contact each other unless it\u2019s an \u201cofficial\u201d matter.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Conclave of the Unbroken Shield holds significant power in the Bound community, though they are often underestimated. Though their numbers and combat training are inferior to the Sanguine Conclave\u2019s, they excel in the area of strategy, and their prowess with defensive manifestations is second to none. Wardens often come into conflict with the Conclave of Aether, who seeks to treasure rare supernatural artefacts that the Conclave of the Unbroken Shield would rather see destroyed.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Wardens gain 1 to 5 Plasm whenever their vice or virtue shines through in the protection of others (for example, a Fortitudinous warden enduring torture to buy time for her companions, or a Greedy warden committing some grand theft in order to draw attention to herself and provide a distraction for her allies).</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Wardens have a +1 bonus to Resolve, Composure and Stamina rolls made to resist supernatural effects.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Wardens may purchase dots in the Shroud manifestation for New Dots x 5 rather than New Dots x 6.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Crossovers:</u></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Supernatural creatures affiliated with this conclave include hunters and changelings.</span></span></span></div></div></div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Conclave of Second Chances</span></i></span></span><br /> <div align=\"left\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Conclave of Second Chances is a relatively modern group, dating back merely decades ago, to the sixties. Generally disregarded by older conclaves, it has been steadily increasing in numbers, until it currently stands as the most populated conclave in Bound society. Its members call themselves celebrants, and seek to use the second chance they have been given to make the most out of their (un)life. Much like the Conclave of Aether, it resembles more a loosely affiliated club than a proper organisation, and most of the other conclaves resent the power they wield in the Bound community simply for having such a plentiful membership.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div></div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Admittance into the conclave is extremely easy and has no requirements. Celebrants throw lively parties to welcome any new member and they are rather open to outsiders. The Conclave of Second Chances believes in encouraging geists to avoid making the same mistakes they made in life and, in due time, to embrace the afterlife without regrets and a smile on one\u2019s face. Celebrants can be travellers, hedonists, socialites or all of the above, and they often throw themselves fully at what they do, attempting to live without regrets and treasuring every joyful moment in their memory.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Socially adroit and never shying away from trying new things, celebrants specialise in manipulation, and though other conclaves consider them unskilled, their ability to control and influence is unmatched. The joie de vivre that pulses inside a celebrant focuses their will, and their constant connection with their own feelings and desires allows them to sharpen their intentions. Combining both will and intention provides the celebrants with a strong force of personality.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Celebrants gain 1 to 5 Plasm whenever their vice or virtue shines through a moment of important celebration (for example, a Hopeful celebrant throwing a party to lift her Pact\u2019s spirits after a failure, or a Gluttonous celebrant indulging in a feast after taking out a great enemy).</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Celebrants have a +1 bonus on Empathy, Socialise, Expression and Intimidation rolls.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Celebrants may purchase dots in the Marionette manifestation for New Dots x 5 rather than New Dots x 6.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Crossovers:</u></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Supernatural creatures affiliated with this conclave include vampires and changelings.</span></span></span></div></div></div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Conclave of Life/Death\u2019s Due</span></i></span></span><br /> <div align=\"left\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Conclave of Life (or the Conclave of Death\u2019s Due, as it is also commonly known) is quite possibly one of the oldest of all conclaves, according to most sources, but is by far the least liked. While other conclaves are in general willing to work together for a common goal, the Conclave of Death\u2019s Due is quite happy to scorn politics and demand a steep compensation for its services. Made up of the malcontent, the rebels, the spiteful and the outcasts, it\u2019s a Conclave that lacks any substantial amount of goodwill towards humanity or their fellow geists.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div></div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Its members used to call themselves advocates in olden times (and some still do), but they have been called bonepickers for long enough that most of its members have started adopting the moniker \u201cironically.\u201d Admittance into the conclave is easy. All one must do is some act of sabotage or rebellion towards the other conclaves. The more spiteful and petty, the better. Welcome ceremonies are usually common and involve revelling in the mayhem caused.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Bonepickers are disdained in Bound society, but their services are often worth bargaining for. The Conclave of Life is a very tightly-knit community and its members tend to find important items, information or supernatural power in their hands. While some advocates are too proud or stubborn to negotiate, most enjoy the power such bargain chips give them over the other conclaves.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Bonepickers gain 1 to 5 Plasm whenever their vice or virtue shines through in a moment of spite (for example, a Faithful bonepicker avenging a minor sacrilege, or a Slothful advocate choosing to stay at home and watch TV when she knows someone she dislikes will be in trouble).</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Bonepickers have a +1 bonus on Wits, Dexterity or Manipulation rolls to acquire things they shouldn\u2019t (such as information, items, lore, etc.).</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Advocates may purchase dots in the Curse manifestation for New Dots x 5 rather than New Dots x 6.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Crossovers:</u></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Supernatural creatures affiliated with this conclave include werewolves, Prometheans and hunters.</span></span></span></div></div></div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Veiled Conclave</span></i></span></span><br /> <div align=\"left\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Nobody truly knows when the Veiled Conclave was originally founded, but the most reputable sources place the first sign of their activity around the first World War, though they didn\u2019t truly become a force to be reckoned with until the Cold War. Members of the Veiled Conclave call themselves gatekeepers, and they take upon themselves to perform the shadier actions that the Bound society needs done.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div></div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Someone finds out confidential information for the Conclave of Aether. Someone watches the shadows while the celebrants enjoy themselves. Someone takes out a target that the Sanguine Conclave can\u2019t assault directly. Someone tips the wardens off of a particular danger they miss. Someone keeps the Gravestone Conclave informed of the latest events in the Bound community. Someone bargains with the bonepickers. The gatekeepers do all this and more. Their power comes from how necessary they are for geist society to function as smoothly as it does, but it\u2019s a fragile thing. While the Veiled Conclave may command power if it acts as a coordinated group, the opinion of individual gatekeepers does not hold much weight when compared to any of the other conclaves.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">To say that they have eyes and ears everywhere is a gross overstatement. The efficiency of their communication networks surpasses the seekers\u2019, yes, but their numbers are far smaller than they\u2019d like to admit. Gaining membership into the Veiled Conclave is almost as hard as getting into the Conclave of the Unbroken Shield, though the process is similar. A current gatekeeper in good standing must vouch for any new candidate, and she needs the full approval of all gatekeepers in the region to gain entrance into the conclave. Once she has been admitted, new gatekeepers are treated to a small welcome party. Gatekeepers may seem callous to outsiders, but they are quite different among each other or towards those they hold dear.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Gatekeepers are spies, infiltrators, assassins, thieves, reconnaissance experts and information brokers. They are particularly good at achieving their goals without being seen and to cause problems without the cause being traced back to them. Their conclave-wide goals are murky, as they have no official leadership (gatekeepers defer to each other according to how powerful they are, and power in the Veiled Conclave can take many forms). Gatekeepers pursue their regular agendas, until it is time to act in the conclave\u2019s name. The conclave has one motto, which every gatekeeper holds close to heart. \u201cDo what they cannot do.\u201d Of course, interpretation of this philosophy is varied, and is the main source of intra-group conflict for the conclave.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Gatekeepers gain 1 to 5 Plasm whenever they express their vice or virtue through stealth or subterfuge, and in the pursuit of what they consider to be their duty (for example, a Prudent gatekeeper convincing her Pact to follow a more stealthy plan when engaging a mission, or a Lustful gatekeeper seducing a target in order to pry valuable secrets).</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Gatekeepers gain a +1 bonus in all Stealth, Larceny, Streetwise and Subterfuge rolls.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Gatekeepers may purchase dots in the Caul manifestation for New Dots x 5 rather than New Dots x 6.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Crossovers:</u></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Supernatural creatures affiliated with this conclave do not have a clear majority. All major types of supernatural creatures can be found in roughly equal measure.</span></span></span></div></div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Ran out of characters, continuing next post.</span></span></span></b></div> <br /> <br /> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T08:13:21-08:00","id":781146,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><u>Keys and Manifestations</u></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">General:</span></i></span></span> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Geists need to be in a specific form in order to use some manifestations.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Wraith-form-only: Marionette and Curse.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Revenant-form-only: Boneyard, Caul and Oracle.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Either form: Rage and Shroud.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">When a Geist unlocks a Manifestation in Wraith-form, she becomes visible (but still intangible) until the beginning of her next turn.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Stygian Key and the Pit Manifestation will not be in use.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Manifestations:</span></i></span></span> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Activating an Elemental Oracle manifestation is a sin against Anamnesis 9 even if it doesn\u2019t deal Aggravated damage.</div></div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">When a Manifestation grants resistance or immunity to a certain type of damage (for example, the Pyre-Flame Shroud granting immunity to natural fire or the Industrial Shroud granting additional armour vs. man-made weapons), it does not apply if the Bound was killed that way. The weakness of a geist to whatever killed them bypasses all forms of protection save for one specific Ceremony.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Passion Caul has a slight change of flavour and mechanics. The geist changes his body to become more attractive, more imposing or more terrifying. He also becomes supernaturally good at dealing with people. The Passion Caul affects Presence instead of Intelligence at * and Social skills instead of Mental at **. At *****, the Passion Caul is reflavoured as giving the geist complete self-assurance and confidence.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Oracle Manifestation allows the geist to observe supernatural phenomena normally hidden from sight (like Mage Sight or Auspex), even at only one dot.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Stigmata Oracle ****: Allows the geist to find the locations of imminent fatal bloodshed (within the next hour) using the same rules. Stigmata Oracle *****: The geist may project his soul into the Shadow by using the same roll.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A geist cannot unlock the Rage manifestation on a corporeal target while she\u2019s in Wraith form unless she\u2019s manifesting or another power allows her to do so.</span></span></span></div> </div></div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Keys:</span></i></span></span> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Geists begin with one Key granted by their Threshold and then one Key that either fits their personality or reflects an important aspect of their death.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><u>Ceremonies</u></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Eliminations:</span></i></span></span> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Krewe Binding. Dedicate Charm. Fetter\u2019s Binding. Sepulchral Gateway.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Changes:</span></i></span></span> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">All ceremonies may be altered flavour-wise so long as the mechanics are respected and the difficulty of the ceremony is maintained.</div></div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Pass On:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Instead of the Underworld, the ceremony must be performed in Twilight (by geists in Wraith form). May be used on geists. If they do so, the amount of successes are added to the geist\u2019s Resolve + Anamnesis pool when dissolving Anchors. A geist can only benefit from one Pass On ceremony at a time (a Bound may attempt to redo the Ceremony if they want to grant a bigger bonus).</span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Distant Voices, Listening to the Spectral Howl and Dead Voices on Air:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> All of these allows for reliable communication with vanquished geists.</span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Plumbing the Depths:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> This is actually a moment of memory and self-introspection.</span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Warding Circle and Warding the Household:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Affects geists as well as ghosts.</span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Bind Anchor:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Does not affect geists. Instead, see Anchor the Soul.</span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Create Deathly Passage:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Still requires at least 4 participants, but only requires 2 different Thresholds (retains the bonus for additional Thresholds). Instead of creating a gate to the Underworld, it opens a passage to any currently uninhabited location within 2 miles per Psyche dot of the ritualist. The location needs to be associated with fresh death. A mortal must either have died 24 hours before, or be fated to die within the next 24 hours. The passage remains open for 1 hour per Psyche dot of the ritualist. Any number of people may pass through the passage while it remains open, but the passage closes if any non-geist lays eyes on its entrance or exit (blindfolded passage is recommended for non-geists). The ritualist chooses whether to open the gate to a valid location of his choosing or to open it to the nearest location within range that meets the requisites.</span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Dumb Supper:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Affects geists in Wraith form.</span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Wings of the Moth:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Affects vanquished geists. Also affects geists in Wraith form, though it\u2019s rather wasteful/useless to do so outside extremely niche circumstances.</span></span></div> </div></div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Additions:</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Convoking the Bound (*):</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> This ceremony sits at the heart of geist culture. It allows a group of Bound to found a new Pact and a geist to join an existing Pact. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Dice Pool:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Psyche (or Psyche + Presence). </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Action:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Extended (target number of 6 to found a Pact or 3 to join an existing Pact). </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Time Increment:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Once every 10 minutes if founding a Pact or once a turn if joining a Pact. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Dramatic Failure:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> All successes are lost, and the rite is tainted. The geist can never join the particular Pact. Geists attempting to found a Pact must add, subtract, or replace a member before they can perform the ceremony again. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Failure:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> No successes are gained. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Success:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> The geists successfully found a Pact or the Bound successfully joins the Pact. See Founding a Pact for further information. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Exceptional Success:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> No additional benefit. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Suggested Modifiers:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> The geists are performing the ceremony in a location associated with new beginnings (+1). One or more of the individuals joining feels coerced into joining (-2). A geist joins or attempts to found a Pact for the express purpose of harming or betraying it (-5).</span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Quiet Memory\u2019s Echoes (***):</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> This ceremony allows for a Bound to appease the shades that distract her while in Wraith form. To do so, the geist must spend some time alone while in Wraith form speaking to her shades, addressing each in turn and telling them what she thinks they want to hear. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Dice Pool:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Psyche + Manipulation. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Action:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Extended (4 successes). </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Time Increment:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Once per 10 minutes. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Dramatic Failure:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> All successes are lost. The shades grow restless. Their penalties are doubled for a day, and this ceremony may not be performed during that time. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Failure:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> The shades are not listening. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Success:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Successes are gained. Once the target number has been met, the geist gains reprieve from the shades\u2019 distracting effect. She does not take the penalty associated with shades for a full 24 hours since she finishes the Ceremony. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Exceptional Success:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Successes are gained. If the target number has been met, she doubles the duration of her reprieve. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Suggested Modifiers:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> The geist is at peace with all her shades (+2). The geist is in a calm state of mind (+1). The geist has not made peace with most of her shades (-2). The geist is upset in some way (-2). The geist\u2019s relationship with her shades while she was alive was particularly turbulent (-3).</span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Fate\u2019s True Defiance (*****):</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> This ceremony allows for a Bound to make a geist out of a willing deceased person, including fully supernatural creatures (such as a ghost, werewolf, vampire, mage, etc.) and to re-Anchor and regenerate a vanquished geist. It requires the deceased\u2019s corpse (not necessary for a vanquished geist) and the presence of a place, object or person to serve as a new Anchor. The prospective Anchor must be somehow related to the target. The ritual involves whispered callings to the deceased and drawing symbols with the geist\u2019s own Plasm (spending 1 point per roll) over the prospective Anchor and, if present, the corpse. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Dice Pool:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Psyche + Resolve. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Action:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Extended (10 successes). </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Time Increment:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Once per hour. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Dramatic Failure:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> All successes are lost. The ritual goes horribly wrong. Something ancient, evil and not of this world enters the corpse or manifests in the location (Storyteller\u2019s discretion). That specific geist may not perform this Ceremony on that specific target again. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Failure:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> The ritual bears no fruit. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Success:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Successes are gained. Once the target number has been met, a new geist has been created at Psyche 1 and Anamnesis 5. Treat other characteristics as normal. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Exceptional Success:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Successes are gained. If the target number has been met, the geist is created at Psyche 2 and Anamnesis 7 instead. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Suggested Modifiers:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> The prospective Anchor for the vanquished geist was actually one of his previous Anchors (+3). The target and the ritualist were dear friends or lovers (+2). Each day that has gone by since the target\u2019s death (-1).</span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Align the Dark Fates (*****):</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> This ceremony allows for a geist to mark a mortal (who must be unaware of the supernatural) to become one of the Bound. The geist must have a depiction of the target (photograph, painting, sketch, etc.) and a small piece of their body (at least a thimble of whole blood, a small piece of flesh or skin, some fingernail clippings, a lock of hair, etc.). The geist then enters a trance and begins to visualise the target\u2019s near future. She also begins narrating out loud the events she sees in her mind\u2019s eye. When the target is in danger in the vision, the geist\u2019s verbal narration changes from merely recounting the events to actually altering them. She speaks out loud the changes that lead the target to their death and sees in her mind\u2019s eye how they will unfold. Her vision concludes as she watches her target die. Performing this Ceremony is a Sin against Anamnesis 3. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Dice Pool:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Psyche + Manipulation. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Action:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Extended (3 successes). </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Time Increment:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Once per 10 minutes. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Dramatic Failure:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> She misaligns fate horribly. The target from now on imposes a -4 to geists attempting to affect her with this Ceremony. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Failure:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> The geist cannot change fate. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Success:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Successes are gained. When she reaches the target number, the mortal is fated to die and return as one of the Bound within one week\u2019s time, as the geist has foreseen in her vision. His Threshold will be up to the new geist, depending on what part of his death was most impactful to him. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Exceptional Success:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> The geist establishes a sympathetic connection with her victim. Once they have become a geist, she gains a +2 on rolls to attempt to persuade them to do as she suggests. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Suggested Modifiers:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> The geist has uncovered deep personal information about her target (+3). The geist has more of the target\u2019s body than she needs (+1). The parts of the body that the geist uses for the Ceremony are dirty or otherwise tainted (-1). The geist has no knowledge at all of her victim (-2).</span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Anchor the Soul (****):</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Every geist is intimately familiar with this Ceremony, as it allows them to bind themselves to a new Anchor. Its performance varies from individual to individual. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Dice Pool:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Psyche + Anamnesis. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Action:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Extended (5 successes). </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Time Increment:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Once per hour. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Dramatic Failure:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> May not happen, as no negative modifiers can be applied. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Failure:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> The geist does not bind to a new Anchor. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Success:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Successes are gained. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Exceptional Success:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Successes are gained. If the target number has been met, the geist\u2019s sudden reconnection with unlife completely heals all damage and fully refills their Plasm. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Suggested Modifiers:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> The Anchor is of huge significance to the geist (+2). The Anchor is of moderate significance to the geist (+1). The Anchor is somehow related to the geist\u2019s Purpose (+2).</span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Song of Triumph (*****):</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> By singing a song of deep emotional meaning to the geist (which must be related to triumph in some way) out loud, the geist becomes so suffused with life that she temporarily ignores her weakness to whatever killed her. This, unfortunately, impedes her from adopting her resilient undead form. Even if she runs out of Plasm, she automatically spends Willpower to look lifelike. If she\u2019s out of both Plasm and Willpower, she loses a Willpower </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>dot</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> to preserve the lifelike state. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Dice Pool:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Psyche + Presence. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Action:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Extended (8 successes). </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Time Increment:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Once per minute. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Dramatic Failure:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> All successes are lost. Instead of life triumphing over death, the opposite occurs. The geist loses her lifelike appearance and may not regain it for a full 24 hours. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Failure:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> The geist does not triumph over death. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Success:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Successes are gained. Once the target number is reached, the geist no longer takes Aggravated damage from attacks/speeches that emulate the way she died. This protection lasts for a scene. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Exceptional Success:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Successes are gained. If the target number was reached, she automatically remains lifelike when she runs out of Plasm, without having to spend a Willpower point or dot. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Suggested Modifiers:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> The song is explicitly about the triumph of life over death (+3). The song is upbeat, joyful, defiant, angry or courageous (+1). The song is sad, apathetic or depressing (-1). The geist\u2019s mood does not match the song\u2019s (-2).</span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Ghostwalk (**):</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> By ritualistically walking a full circle around her unconscious body and reciting a list of places she visited while she was alive, a geist in Wraith form may extend the time she may spend in Wraith form and the distance she may part from her body. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Dice Pool:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Psyche + Stamina. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Action:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Extended (4 successes). </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Time Increment:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Once per minute. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Dramatic Failure:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> The geist snaps back into her body. She returns to Revenant form and may not go into Wraith form for the rest of the scene. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Failure:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> The geist fails to commence the ghostwalk. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Success:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Successes are gained. If the target number is reached, the geist begins to ghostwalk. She gains a special aura that trails a certain effect behind her, usually related to her personality or Threshold (such as flower petals, ash, dust, metal scrapes, snowflakes, water or blood droplets, etc.). She may remain in Wraith form for 2 hours per point of Psyche, and she may wander up to 100 yards per point of Psyche away from her body. The effects of the ceremony last for the rest of the scene. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Exceptional Success:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Successes are gained. If the target number is reached, her ghostwalk is particularly powerful, allowing her to remain in Wraith form for 3 hours per point of Psyche, and she may wander up to 200 yards per point of Psyche away from her body. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Suggested Modifiers:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Ceremony is performed in a cemetery (+3). The geist has an Elemental Key (+1). The geist is leaving her body in plain sight (-1). The geist\u2019s body has been damaged while she was in Wraith form in the last 24 hours (-5).</span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Veiled Touch (*):</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> By gently caressing the bare skin (usually the face) of a living being who cannot see into Twilight (they may be supernatural being, all that matters is that they are not dead or undead), a Bound in Wraith form may manifest, much like a ghost. The geist may choose to be visible or invisible when she manifests, but regardless of her choice, this allows them to affect the material world while in Wraith form (which is normally impossible save for specific circumstances). In order to exert any significant pressure, the geist must make a Strength roll. Precise motions may require Dexterity rolls at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Dice Pool:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Psyche + Dexterity. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Action:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Extended (3 successes). </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Time Increment:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Once per turn. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Dramatic Failure:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> All successes are lost. The geist disturbs the ambient energies and her Twilight state is rattled. She may not attempt this Ceremony for the rest of the scene, and she takes a -2 to all rolls to unlock Manifestations or perform Ceremonies while in Wraith form. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Failure:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> The geist fails to manifest. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Success:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Successes are gained. Once she attains the target number, she may manifest while in Wraith form at will for a scene. She may also return to Twilight when she pleases. Manifesting and going to Twilight are both reflexive actions. The effects of this Ceremony ends when she returns to Revenant form. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Exceptional Success:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Successes are gained. If she has reached the target number, she may return to Revenant form without ending the effects of this Ceremony, which allows her to switch back and forth between multiple forms and states at will, as is most convenient to her. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Suggested Modifiers:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> The living being is of emotional significance to the geist (+2). The living being is vulnerable and unsuspecting (+1). The geist has the Phantasmal Key (+1). The living being is a supernatural creature (-1). For every additional living creature in the room beyond the target (-1).</span></span></div> </div></div> </div> </div></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><u>Other Rules</u></span></span></span> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Underworld does not exist in these houserules (however, a Storyteller may choose to have the Underworld exist without much fuss). As such, Haunt Fluidity instead applies to rolls for conducting Ceremonies. Abmortals may or may not exist as the Storyteller wishes.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mementos do not exist in these houserules.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Consuming a ghost\u2019s corpus counts as providing a week\u2019s worth of food and water sustenance for the geist.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Haunts generate Plasm per night, not per week.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><u>Founding a Pact</u></span></span></span> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">As per Founding a Krewe, but with the following modifications:</div></div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Replace the word \u201ckrewe\u201d for the word \u201cPact.\u201d Any Pacts may use the Founding and Supernatural benefits of any tier regardless of their size. Instead of the geists being seen as mythical entities, the collective myth instead shapes ideals that the geists wish to aspire towards.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Channeling Aspects and Avatars imposes a penalty on Anamnesis due to the geist temporarily forgetting their sense of self as they are caught up in the ideal they aspire towards.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sending Forth The Aspect instead allows for mental communication between both parties, it allows the target to use the founder\u2019s Keys for any Manifestations they have in common (using all of the target\u2019s characteristics), and it allows the founder to use Keys and Manifestations through the target.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Revenance allows for founders to be resurrected without a loss of Psyche or Anamnesis (and avoiding the death of an innocent), but doing so requires the presence of all founders, a Haunt, a semi-intact body (as described in the book) and for the geists to collectively pour at least 100 total Plasm into the body of their soon-to-be resurrected companion. As per the original Revenance, this fails if the geist was killed the same way it originally died. This works on vanquished geists.</span></span></span></div></div></div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><u>Character Creation</u></span></span></span> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ignore Archetypes. They have been replaced by Conclaves.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">All Geists begin with a point in the Oracle Manifestation for free. The Bound are haunted by dreams of life cut short, by the calls of the dead and by the urge to either defy or enforce Fate. All geists know how to part the veil between life and death and peer through it for answers.<br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> <b>Comments are always welcome, of course.</b></span></span></span></div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":10056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","user":"ShadowKnight1224","date":". 12-06-2015, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T18:32:39-08:00","id":781451,"title":"","content":"It's an interesting take, and I think it's interesting how you cleave closer to Wraith in some ways than the original Geist did. (I always felt that G:tSE was more following Orpheus than Wraith anyway).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T09:28:40-08:00","id":781726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/350125-fan-made-splat-display-show-us-your-stuff?p=781451#post781451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an interesting take, and I think it's interesting how you cleave closer to Wraith in some ways than the original Geist did. (I always felt that G:tSE was more following Orpheus than Wraith anyway).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Geist is my second-favourite line, but I've never really bought the flavour of the book or that whole &quot;devil over your shoulder&quot; thing. I read the original Wraith years ago, but I found it a bit too grim for my tastes. I think the WoD could use a splat that is like Hunter but more individually powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"u